WEBVTT

00:00:01.422 --> 00:00:04.172
(dramatic music)

00:01:13.725 --> 00:01:15.975
(blasting)

00:01:30.449 --> 00:01:32.616
(booming)

00:01:53.945 --> 00:01:55.999
The continued wave of
death-dealing explosions

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.649
struck yesterday at area
defense headquarters

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.809
as in previous occasions
the authorities are unable

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.459
to detect the cause of these blasts

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.539
which have done untold damage.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.239
Who could possibly be doing this?

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.089
Well there are several theories Joan,

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.639
but so far no one is even
sure what kind of explosives

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.789
are being used or how they're set off.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:14.639
Maybe Mr. Henderson will
have some information

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.289
for us when he gets in from Washington.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.799
That guy Henderson wouldn't
tell you what time it is.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.519
Just what is his job anyway?

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.739
He won't tell you that
either Ted, it's a big one.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.459
He only answers to a few
people in this country of ours.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:27.830
I think that... (knocking)

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.469
Hello Mr. Henderson.
-Hello Commander Cody.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:34.139
Ted, Miss Gilbert.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.579
How are you getting along
with the rocket ship?

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.359
As well as can be expected sir.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.499
Our test with the model is satisfactory.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.059
If the government will
let us make a few test

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:41.893
flights with the rocket...

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:43.199
It's out of the question.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.300
This whole project is strictly top-secret.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.879
Since you people developed the rocket ship

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.259
for us and we'll be the ones operating it,

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.589
it has been decided that you
should know more of our plans.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.869
I've been authorized to tell you this much:

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.339
its primary use will be to combat this wave

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.189
of sabotage and destruction
of our defense system.

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.219
You mean the government
knows what's causing it?

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.609
Not definitely, but tests
of the wreckage show that

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.709
the explosions are of atomic origin.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.169
You mean someone's
dropping atomic bombs on us?

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.979
Not bombs; No planes have been observed,

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:13.869
and the explosions aren't severe enough.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:15.359
No, from what I've learned of the nature of

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.759
the blast they see more like
an atomic ray of some kind.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.389
Of course that's just a guess.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.429
It's the same guess that we've made

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.629
because it's the only possible answer.

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:24.949
[Cody] But no one has ever been able to

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.469
make an atomic ray machine.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.869
You mean no one on earth ever has.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.489
Say, this rocket we're
building we'll be able

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.579
to fly to the moon, maybe someone up there's

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.009
built one that could get down here.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.789
We believe that possible,

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.769
and for some time our
astronomers have been noticing

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:41.019
an unusual amount of atomic
activity on the moon.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.139
Atomic activity on the moon.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.869
Atomic blasts on the Earth.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.919
The two known facts fit together.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:48.960
Yes, it adds up.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:51.989
So that's why you want
us to fly to the moon.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:54.099
Yes, and when you get to the moon find out

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.329
if these attacks are
actually coming from there

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.129
and try to devise some
plan for stopping them.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.610
In the meantime we'll do we
can with these attacks here.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.859
Is your flying suit still working?

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.149
Yes.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:08.199
We may ask you to use it.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.139
If a ray gun is being used
to cause these blasts,

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.619
it's probably being operated from the ground

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.919
and if you could get to the scene of

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.599
the attack soon enough,

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:19.169
you might be able to find
some clue to the attackers.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.259
I'll be glad to try.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.789
Good, we'll phone you as soon as we

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.469
have any information about another attack.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:24.303
All right, sir.

00:04:24.304 --> 00:04:25.363
-Goodbye.
-Goodbye.

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:28.947
(light instrumental music)

00:04:30.908 --> 00:04:33.491
(horn honking)

00:04:37.802 --> 00:04:40.302
There she is, right on time.

00:04:42.758 --> 00:04:47.758
(blasting) (dramatic music)

00:04:47.809 --> 00:04:48.791
(chuckling)

00:04:48.792 --> 00:04:50.140
Well, that did it.

00:04:50.141 --> 00:04:51.309
Let's get over to Kern Pass.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.110
That troop train will be along soon.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:59.019
All right I'll get out there right away.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:00.239
Say, give me a hand with
the flying suit, Ted.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.329
Sure.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.759
A trainload of army supplies was just

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.939
blasted off the west end of the valley.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.359
A rancher reported he saw a truck parked on

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.139
a hill overlooking the
tracks with two men in it.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:12.469
Working some kind of a gun.

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:13.569
They pulled out right after the wreck

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:15.519
and headed toward Kern Hills.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:17.449
Henderson's office gave a
description of the trucks

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.539
and I'm going out to look for it.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.299
I suppose you'll be wanting this.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.020
Yes I may need it.

00:05:28.626 --> 00:05:31.876
(light dramatic music)

00:05:40.936 --> 00:05:43.186
(blasting)

00:06:02.627 --> 00:06:05.627
She ought to be along anytime now.

00:06:13.304 --> 00:06:15.554
(chugging)

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:21.190
Okay get set.

00:06:59.139 --> 00:07:00.068
Now!

00:07:00.069 --> 00:07:02.235
(banging)

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.149
Let's get out of here!

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:23.130
And leave the ray gun?

00:07:23.131 --> 00:07:24.230
What else can we do?

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.929
The loss of the ray gun is not too serious.

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:43.179
I brought sufficient equipment from

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:44.859
the moon to build several of them

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:46.889
but I do not care to have
the Earth people learn

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:48.270
the secrets of our weapons.

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:50.679
From the description you gave me of

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.809
your attackers costume it must have

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:55.010
been Commando Cody in his flying suit.

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:57.799
He will probably take our ray gun to his

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.979
laboratory for examination

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.529
so you must go there at once and recover

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:03.769
the atomic chamber from the ray gun.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:05.170
That's a large order Krog.

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:08.749
We hired out to work your
ray gun, this business...

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:09.989
You were hired to do anything

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:11.799
that I may consider necessary to pave

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.750
the way for our invasion from the moon.

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:15.949
You're being well paid for your work,

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.240
so do as you're ordered.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:19.343
Okay.

00:08:25.045 --> 00:08:28.295
(light dramatic music)

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.119
Is working on this gun going to hold

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.509
up finishing the rocket ship?

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.799
No, I'll just give it a quick examination

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.789
and then turn it over to the authorities.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.280
We'll still be able to take off
for the moon next Wednesday.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:53.350
Take it easy and you won't get hurt.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:55.593
Move back.

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:58.763
There's the unit we want, grab it.

00:09:01.219 --> 00:09:05.018
(dramatic music) (clattering)

00:09:05.019 --> 00:09:07.269
(grunting)

00:09:09.334 --> 00:09:11.584
(thudding)

00:09:18.917 --> 00:09:21.084
(banging)

00:10:07.634 --> 00:10:08.993
And don't try to follow us.

00:10:21.062 --> 00:10:24.145
(light spooky music)

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.320
[Krog] Krog Calling Retik.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:37.100
Krog calling Retik.

00:10:46.385 --> 00:10:47.519
Come in, Krog.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:49.699
A rocket ship is leaving here in five days

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.409
to investigate our moon.

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:53.019
I did not believe the earth men possessed

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.209
a ship capable of making the journey.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:56.859
I just learned about it myself

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:58.939
but I'm sure my information is correct.

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:01.119
Very well, it is not too serious.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:02.469
We will be prepared to take care of

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:03.970
the visitors when they arrive.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:34.469
I still think this is no trip for a woman.

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:35.749
Now don't start that again,

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.429
you'll be very glad to have someone along

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:38.589
who can cook your meals.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:39.580
I'll say we will.

00:11:39.581 --> 00:11:41.079
Don't give her any more arguments.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:42.640
Okay, I like to eat too.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:55.069
Well boys that's it.

00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:57.479
Well the best of luck to all of you sir.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.499
Hope this thing works all right.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:00.380
So do we.

00:12:00.381 --> 00:12:01.870
See ya, bye.
-Goodbye, sir.

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:09.490
Hiya, folks.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:10.323
Hello Hank.

00:12:10.324 --> 00:12:11.439
All set?

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:12.999
All warmed up, we can take off right now,

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.149
that is if the ship will stand up to

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.359
the test we made with the model.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:16.439
I think it will.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:17.273
Now, let's go.

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:30.710
Safety belts fastened?

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.157
Fire pilot jets.

00:12:35.158 --> 00:12:39.769
(air hissing) (light dramatic music)

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:40.780
Fire main jets!

00:12:43.033 --> 00:12:45.283
(whirring)

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:13.579
Right, well you'd hardly
know we were moving.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:14.580
Well, believe it or not we are.

00:13:14.581 --> 00:13:16.439
A lot of miles per minute.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.379
She's living up to the test we made.

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:19.719
Set a course for the moon.

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:20.553
Right.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.080
Take over here, will ya, Ted?

00:13:28.295 --> 00:13:31.795
(light suspenseful music)

00:13:52.362 --> 00:13:54.195
We're just about here.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:01.859
Looks like we're on the right track.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.790
We ought to be down in another two hours.

00:14:10.698 --> 00:14:12.948
(whirring)

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:15.440
There's a city just ahead.

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:20.570
[Hank] Where do we sit down?

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:24.009
Let's take her back in those hills where

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:25.810
we can find a place to hide the ship

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:28.919
and I'll fly over the city in the rocket suit.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:29.753
Okay.

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:40.565
Settle down in that canyon.

00:14:40.566 --> 00:14:45.566
Okay.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:04.167
(clattering)

00:15:18.782 --> 00:15:23.782
(blasting) (light dramatic music)

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:46.459
You are going in the
right direction, Earth man.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.150
Enter the first door you come to.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.730
Turn the control, the door will open.

00:16:01.585 --> 00:16:03.835
(creaking)

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:38.180
Welcome, Commando Cody.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:51.929
I am Retik, ruler of the Moon.

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:53.659
Apparently you are expecting me.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:54.679
Of course.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:57.249
For many years our radio
has kept us informed

00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:59.839
of events on Earth and my men there

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:01.590
have advised me of your every move.

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:04.529
I see you have adopted our language.

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:08.109
Yes, all our people are
required to speak English

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:10.660
so we can operate more
efficiently in your country.

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:13.999
You mind telling me why
your men are carrying out

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:16.299
that campaign of destruction on Earth?

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:17.290
Not at all.

00:17:17.291 --> 00:17:19.159
They are merely softening up your defenses

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.880
for our impending invasion.

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:24.329
Why do you want to invade the earth?

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:26.529
Because the atmosphere
on the moon has become

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:28.969
so thin and dry it is impossible for us

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:32.739
to raise food except in
pressurized greenhouses

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:35.319
and none of us can move
outside without helmets

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:38.369
so we are planning a mass
migration to your world.

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:41.419
You will find that conquering
the earth isn't so simple.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:45.919
Ah, but it will be because
of our atomic weapons

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:48.559
on the Moon we have an element, Lunarian,

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:51.569
which is far superior to uranium as a base

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:55.239
for atomic reactions and
we can completely control

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:57.999
the force of these reactions enabling us

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:01.629
to build atomic weapons
ranging from huge cannon

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:03.290
to these small ray pistols.

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:10.869
It's very considerate of you

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:13.079
to give me all this information.

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:16.199
You deserve some reward
for your long journey,

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.569
but unfortunately I cannot permit you

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.419
to return to Earth with it.

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:22.786
Maybe I have something to say about that.

00:18:22.787 --> 00:18:25.537
(dramatic music)

00:18:26.875 --> 00:18:29.125
(whirring)

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:33.719
So much for the
effectiveness of your weapons.

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:36.420
Now I will demonstrate one of ours.

00:18:41.051 --> 00:18:42.283
(blasting)

00:18:42.284 --> 00:18:45.034
(dramatic music)

00:18:46.026 --> 00:18:49.226
Seize him!

00:18:49.227 --> 00:18:51.644
(clattering)

00:18:58.783 --> 00:19:01.033
(thudding)

00:19:23.115 --> 00:19:25.365
(blasting)

00:19:35.575 --> 00:19:37.992
(clattering)

00:19:52.845 --> 00:19:54.933
(blasting)

00:19:54.934 --> 00:19:57.684
(dramatic music)

00:21:39.112 --> 00:21:43.612
(thudding) (blasting)

00:21:50.380 --> 00:21:52.797
(clattering)

00:22:08.906 --> 00:22:11.073
(booming)

00:22:19.421 --> 00:22:21.671
(creaking)

00:22:40.633 --> 00:22:45.633
(blasting) (light dramatic music)

00:23:10.004 --> 00:23:11.910
(buzzing)

00:23:12.210 --> 00:23:13.859
So Retik plans to invade the Earth

00:23:13.860 --> 00:23:15.419
with his army from the Moon.

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:16.549
As soon as the saboteur's,

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:18.989
he already has their finish
softening up our defenses.

00:23:18.990 --> 00:23:20.559
Do you think he'll be able to do it?

00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:21.969
I'm afraid he might.

00:23:21.970 --> 00:23:24.249
I don't know how many men
or rocket ships he has,

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:26.629
but his atomic weapons are
so far ahead of anything

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:28.809
we have he wouldn't need a very big army.

00:23:28.810 --> 00:23:31.029
What did you find out about the ray guns?

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:33.249
Only that they use an
element called Lumarium.

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:36.499
Instead of uranium as the base
for their atomic reactions.

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:38.339
They apparently can control the reaction

00:23:38.340 --> 00:23:40.899
so they will work either
as a disintegrating ray

00:23:40.900 --> 00:23:43.109
or as an explosion like our atomic bomb.

00:23:43.110 --> 00:23:44.569
Well if their weapons are that powerful

00:23:44.570 --> 00:23:47.509
it would be impossible for
our people to attack them here

00:23:47.510 --> 00:23:50.379
even if we had rockets
enough to transport an army.

00:23:50.380 --> 00:23:51.589
That's right.

00:23:51.590 --> 00:23:53.749
Apparently they let us land
because they weren't afraid

00:23:53.750 --> 00:23:56.059
of a single ship but they
would undoubtedly blast

00:23:56.060 --> 00:23:57.359
it at an invading fleet.

00:23:57.360 --> 00:23:58.659
Then hadn't we better go back right

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:00.359
away and warn our people?

00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:02.189
Our orders were to find out if the attacks

00:24:02.190 --> 00:24:03.969
were coming from here and if so,

00:24:03.970 --> 00:24:05.819
to try to figure out some way to stop them.

00:24:05.820 --> 00:24:06.999
And those are large orders.

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:09.559
All we have is a light machine
gun and some hand grenades.

00:24:09.560 --> 00:24:11.399
They wouldn't do much to that walled city.

00:24:11.400 --> 00:24:14.029
No, but there was one of their ray guns

00:24:14.030 --> 00:24:15.549
in Retik's laboratory.

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:17.479
If I could get hold of that it would be easy

00:24:17.480 --> 00:24:19.339
to blast open their pressurized buildings

00:24:19.340 --> 00:24:20.919
and really put them out of business.

00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:22.699
All you've gotta do is get the gun.

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:24.389
That may not be too tough.

00:24:24.390 --> 00:24:26.639
We brought some nitrous
oxide with us, didn't we?

00:24:26.640 --> 00:24:28.290
Yes there's a small tank of it.

00:24:33.070 --> 00:24:35.799
I'll find the air-intake that
leads to Retik's laboratory

00:24:35.800 --> 00:24:38.399
and turn the gas into it, that
ought to put them to sleep

00:24:38.400 --> 00:24:40.629
long enough to let me
get away with a ray gun.

00:24:40.630 --> 00:24:42.039
If it's like the gun you found on Earth

00:24:42.040 --> 00:24:44.319
it'll be too heavy to
carry, let alone fly with.

00:24:44.320 --> 00:24:46.739
That's right, but the tripod isn't important.

00:24:46.740 --> 00:24:48.699
I'll dismantle a gun from the tripod.

00:24:48.700 --> 00:24:50.469
I think I can handle a gun all right.

00:24:50.470 --> 00:24:52.289
Maybe you can but it'll be quite a load.

00:24:52.290 --> 00:24:53.859
I better get a helmet and go with you.

00:24:53.860 --> 00:24:56.569
Hank and Joan can stay
here and guard the ship.

00:24:56.570 --> 00:24:58.580
Okay, I may need some help with that.

00:25:01.300 --> 00:25:04.800
(light suspenseful music)

00:25:18.602 --> 00:25:20.319
You better not come any closer.

00:25:20.320 --> 00:25:22.049
I'll fly on in and get the gun.

00:25:22.050 --> 00:25:24.469
I'll manage to lug it back this far myself.

00:25:24.470 --> 00:25:26.139
[Ted] With the whole town chasing you?

00:25:26.140 --> 00:25:27.669
[Cody] I don't think
they can get around outside

00:25:27.670 --> 00:25:29.400
very well, but we'll find out.

00:25:33.239 --> 00:25:36.448
(dramatic music)

00:25:36.449 --> 00:25:38.699
(blasting)

00:26:38.100 --> 00:26:40.689
Nesor, something's wrong
the ventilating system.

00:26:40.690 --> 00:26:41.530
Get the oxygen.

00:26:44.509 --> 00:26:46.759
(thudding)

00:26:56.836 --> 00:26:59.086
(creaking)

00:27:03.474 --> 00:27:04.756
(clanking)

00:27:04.757 --> 00:27:07.507
(dramatic music)

00:27:50.371 --> 00:27:52.621
(grunting)

00:27:55.223 --> 00:27:57.473
(thudding)

00:28:35.904 --> 00:28:38.154
(crashing)

00:28:55.936 --> 00:28:58.103
(buzzing)

00:29:11.864 --> 00:29:13.459
Guards, guards!

00:29:13.460 --> 00:29:14.889
The Earth man has escaped with a ray gun,

00:29:14.890 --> 00:29:16.764
send a car out to search for him.

00:29:16.765 --> 00:29:19.015
(rumbling)

00:29:38.520 --> 00:29:39.969
-You got it.
-Yeah.

00:29:39.970 --> 00:29:41.419
But it sure is heavy.

00:29:41.420 --> 00:29:43.149
-Is anybody after you?
-Not yet.

00:29:43.150 --> 00:29:44.120
Give me a hand with this.

00:29:44.121 --> 00:29:45.631
We've got to move fast.

00:29:45.632 --> 00:29:49.715
(suspenseful instrumental music)

00:29:52.213 --> 00:29:54.463
(rumbling)

00:29:57.998 --> 00:29:58.840
[Guard] He must have come this way,

00:29:58.841 --> 00:30:01.589
he couldn't have got by the
guards at the canyon bridge.

00:30:01.590 --> 00:30:04.590
[Guard] No, and he won't move
very fast carrying that gun.

00:30:14.081 --> 00:30:15.781
There they are, give them a blast.

00:30:17.610 --> 00:30:19.860
(blasting)

00:30:20.830 --> 00:30:22.079
[Ted] What do we do now?

00:30:22.080 --> 00:30:23.699
[Cody] Let's try to keep going.

00:30:23.700 --> 00:30:26.070
Maybe we could dodge around
those rocks and lose them.

00:30:53.730 --> 00:30:56.200
[Ted] They're still after us, let's go.

00:31:09.680 --> 00:31:12.040
[Cody] That looks like a
cave, let's get in there.

00:31:34.690 --> 00:31:37.199
[Guard] We can't follow them in there.

00:31:37.200 --> 00:31:38.609
Set the ray gun at constant heat,

00:31:38.610 --> 00:31:41.229
it will melt the cliff and bury them alive.

00:31:41.230 --> 00:31:44.000
Right. (Dramatic music)

00:32:16.130 --> 00:32:17.472
[Ted] What's that?

00:32:17.473 --> 00:32:18.659
[Cody] They turned the ray gun into the side

00:32:18.660 --> 00:32:20.736
of the cave and it's melting the rock.

00:32:20.737 --> 00:32:22.634
Let's get back as far as we can.

00:32:22.635 --> 00:32:24.603
Never mind the gun!

00:32:24.604 --> 00:32:27.354
(dramatic music)

00:33:05.834 --> 00:33:10.834
[Guard] That will finish them.

00:33:20.297 --> 00:33:23.047
(dramatic music)

00:35:00.176 --> 00:35:05.176
(suspenseful music) (bubbling)

00:35:25.100 --> 00:35:26.899
[Cody] Maybe we can get out along that side.

00:35:26.900 --> 00:35:28.429
[Ted] But what about that tank?

00:35:28.430 --> 00:35:30.580
[Cody] We may be able to take care of it.

00:35:37.596 --> 00:35:40.596
(suspenseful music)

00:35:46.140 --> 00:35:47.177
Let's try this one.

00:36:00.450 --> 00:36:01.800
[Guard] That will finish them.

00:36:03.300 --> 00:36:04.540
[Cody] Get me a hand grenade.

00:36:12.688 --> 00:36:14.855
(booming)

00:36:16.069 --> 00:36:17.050
[Guard] They must have gotten out,

00:36:17.051 --> 00:36:18.200
let's move out of here.

00:36:19.232 --> 00:36:21.482
(rumbling)

00:36:31.680 --> 00:36:32.719
[Cody] That does it Ted,

00:36:32.720 --> 00:36:34.290
let's get back to the rocket ship.

00:36:41.530 --> 00:36:43.459
Too bad you lost that ray gun.

00:36:43.460 --> 00:36:45.259
You'll have a tough time
getting another one now.

00:36:45.260 --> 00:36:46.509
We haven't a chance of getting one,

00:36:46.510 --> 00:36:48.089
and we couldn't possibly attack their city

00:36:48.090 --> 00:36:49.339
with any of our weapons.

00:36:49.340 --> 00:36:50.829
That isn't the worst of it.

00:36:50.830 --> 00:36:52.249
They've already tracked us halfway to

00:36:52.250 --> 00:36:54.119
this ship so they know about where we are.

00:36:54.120 --> 00:36:56.179
It's only a question of
time until they find us.

00:36:56.180 --> 00:36:57.429
One blast from that ray gun

00:36:57.430 --> 00:36:59.569
will pop this ship like a toy balloon.

00:36:59.570 --> 00:37:01.370
Maybe we better get back to earth.

00:37:03.440 --> 00:37:04.789
I think so.

00:37:04.790 --> 00:37:07.539
We've accomplished the most
important part of our mission;

00:37:07.540 --> 00:37:09.299
we discovered that Retik is planning to lead

00:37:09.300 --> 00:37:10.729
an invasion from the moon as soon as the

00:37:10.730 --> 00:37:13.349
saboteurs finish softening up our defenses,

00:37:13.350 --> 00:37:15.919
and it's up to us to get that
information back to Earth.

00:37:15.920 --> 00:37:17.399
How soon can we take off?

00:37:17.400 --> 00:37:18.759
Well I've gotta build
up the pressure in all the

00:37:18.760 --> 00:37:21.249
tanks and warm up the
jets, maybe a couple hours.

00:37:21.250 --> 00:37:22.989
Then get started.

00:37:22.990 --> 00:37:25.767
I'll fly out and scout
around until you're ready.

00:37:25.768 --> 00:37:29.268
(light suspenseful music)

00:37:47.343 --> 00:37:49.419
(clicking)

00:37:49.420 --> 00:37:52.189
Scout Seven reporting to headquarters.

00:37:52.190 --> 00:37:53.980
Scout Seven reporting to headquarters.

00:37:55.300 --> 00:37:56.133
Come in.

00:37:56.134 --> 00:37:58.519
I found the earth man's
rocket ship, Your Excellency,

00:37:58.520 --> 00:38:00.539
it's in a canyon only about a mile west

00:38:00.540 --> 00:38:02.679
where our scout car was attacked.

00:38:02.680 --> 00:38:03.949
Splendid.

00:38:03.950 --> 00:38:06.439
I'll send another car out after it at once.

00:38:06.440 --> 00:38:07.809
Stay there and keep watch.

00:38:07.810 --> 00:38:08.760
[Scout] Yes, sir.

00:38:11.415 --> 00:38:16.415
(blasting) (dramatic music)

00:38:33.178 --> 00:38:35.428
(thudding)

00:38:58.013 --> 00:39:00.263
(smacking)

00:39:10.686 --> 00:39:12.936
(blasting)

00:39:24.359 --> 00:39:26.077
The scout found our ship.

00:39:26.078 --> 00:39:28.529
I took care of 'em but I'm
afraid he already reported us.

00:39:28.530 --> 00:39:30.549
How much longer before we can take off?

00:39:30.550 --> 00:39:32.470
[Ted] One of those tanks is headed this way!

00:39:34.300 --> 00:39:35.359
How 'bout it, Hank?

00:39:35.360 --> 00:39:37.559
I won't guarantee the
results but we can try.

00:39:37.560 --> 00:39:39.518
Here it goes, all jets.

00:39:39.519 --> 00:39:41.686
(hissing)

00:39:47.827 --> 00:39:51.327
(light suspenseful music)

00:39:53.980 --> 00:39:55.579
Looks like we may make it.

00:39:55.580 --> 00:39:58.086
If we get out of range
of that ray gun in time.

00:39:58.087 --> 00:40:00.337
(rumbling)

00:40:02.637 --> 00:40:04.804
(booming)

00:40:15.118 --> 00:40:16.259
(rumbling)

00:40:16.260 --> 00:40:17.860
Shut off that induction valve!

00:40:28.260 --> 00:40:29.769
Protect the other compartments.

00:40:29.770 --> 00:40:30.603
Right!

00:40:36.700 --> 00:40:38.950
(blasting)

00:40:41.049 --> 00:40:42.409
Well, that one barely reached us.

00:40:42.410 --> 00:40:43.880
Looks like we're in the clear.

00:40:45.210 --> 00:40:46.060
Things are sort of messed up

00:40:46.061 --> 00:40:47.560
in there, but nothing serious.

00:40:48.950 --> 00:40:51.479
Okay, Hank, you can start for the earth now.

00:40:51.480 --> 00:40:52.750
Make a 180 degree turn.

00:40:53.590 --> 00:40:54.789
Right, Commando.

00:40:54.790 --> 00:40:55.623
Homeward bound.

00:41:08.140 --> 00:41:08.973
Very well.

00:41:10.750 --> 00:41:13.300
Patrol car reported that
the spaceship has escaped.

00:41:14.330 --> 00:41:16.780
That ship must not be
allowed to land on Earth.

00:41:21.600 --> 00:41:22.720
Retik to Krog.

00:41:22.721 --> 00:41:25.221
(light music)

00:41:29.810 --> 00:41:30.989
Retik to Krog.

00:41:30.990 --> 00:41:32.249
Come in, Retik.

00:41:32.250 --> 00:41:34.639
Commano Cody's rocket ship has escaped

00:41:34.640 --> 00:41:36.109
and is headed back to Earth.

00:41:36.110 --> 00:41:38.789
He has all the information
about our planned invasion

00:41:38.790 --> 00:41:41.449
and must not be allowed to
tell it to the authorities.

00:41:41.450 --> 00:41:44.819
Will you have a ray gun
completed by the time he lands?

00:41:44.820 --> 00:41:47.099
I'm afraid that is
impossible, Your Excellency.

00:41:47.100 --> 00:41:49.999
[Retik] Then use of bomb
any other weapon available.

00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:51.629
That ship must be destroyed before

00:41:51.630 --> 00:41:53.479
anyone could get out of it.

00:41:53.480 --> 00:41:54.580
Yes, Your Excellency.

00:41:58.720 --> 00:42:00.389
You heard the orders.

00:42:00.390 --> 00:42:02.289
Yeah but it might not be that easy.

00:42:02.290 --> 00:42:04.099
There may be guards at the landing field.

00:42:04.100 --> 00:42:06.769
Nevertheless you will
carry out instructions.

00:42:06.770 --> 00:42:08.709
I will furnish you with a bomb,

00:42:08.710 --> 00:42:10.359
you can devise some means for placing

00:42:10.360 --> 00:42:12.659
it under the ship the moment it lands.

00:42:12.660 --> 00:42:14.449
How do we know when they'll get here?

00:42:14.450 --> 00:42:17.009
I'll pick up their approach on my radar

00:42:17.010 --> 00:42:19.060
so you can be in position when they land.

00:42:20.107 --> 00:42:22.607
(light music)

00:42:40.504 --> 00:42:41.780
Just like we figured.

00:42:41.980 --> 00:42:45.049
Yes, we've got to blast them, then plant

00:42:45.050 --> 00:42:47.300
the bomb before anyone
can get out of a ship.

00:42:51.210 --> 00:42:52.060
Here she comes.

00:42:52.905 --> 00:42:55.155
(rumbling)

00:42:56.720 --> 00:42:57.970
Going in for a landing.

00:43:08.500 --> 00:43:09.909
Calling landing field.

00:43:09.910 --> 00:43:11.369
Calling landing field.

00:43:11.370 --> 00:43:13.249
Landing field to rocket, come in.

00:43:13.250 --> 00:43:14.190
We're coming down.

00:43:14.191 --> 00:43:15.319
Is the field clear?

00:43:15.320 --> 00:43:17.070
Yes, sir we're all ready for you.

00:43:22.310 --> 00:43:24.560
All right, Hank, make your 180 degree turn.

00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:34.957
You take the one on the right.

00:43:37.908 --> 00:43:42.825
(banging) (dramatic music)

00:44:27.710 --> 00:44:29.110
Let's get over to the car!

00:44:39.355 --> 00:44:43.355
We'll never make it
now, let's get outta here.

00:44:49.060 --> 00:44:51.389
(rumbling)

00:44:51.390 --> 00:44:52.280
They're taking off in a car.

00:44:52.281 --> 00:44:54.840
I'm gonna go after them, you guard the ship!

00:44:56.801 --> 00:44:59.634
(engine rumbling)

00:45:10.810 --> 00:45:12.360
They're after us, step on it!

00:45:21.830 --> 00:45:24.747
(tires screeching)

00:45:30.165 --> 00:45:34.110
He's hanging onto us, give it all you can.

00:46:00.223 --> 00:46:05.223
Stop on that bridge!

00:46:10.529 --> 00:46:13.916
(tires screeching)

00:46:13.917 --> 00:46:17.334
(frantic dramatic music)

00:46:36.886 --> 00:46:39.053
(hissing)

00:46:40.006 --> 00:46:42.173
(booming)

00:46:46.742 --> 00:46:49.492
(dramatic music)

00:48:21.875 --> 00:48:23.792
(tires screeching)

00:48:29.571 --> 00:48:31.166
Stop on that bridge!

00:48:31.466 --> 00:48:34.716
(light dramatic music)

00:48:57.222 --> 00:48:59.389
(screeching)

00:49:03.487 --> 00:49:03.954
(booming)

00:49:09.022 --> 00:49:10.555
(splashing)

00:49:17.850 --> 00:49:19.829
So the people on the Moon are planning

00:49:19.830 --> 00:49:21.559
a direct attack on the world as soon as

00:49:21.560 --> 00:49:24.566
their saboteurs have
softened up our defenses.

00:49:24.567 --> 00:49:26.279
What do you think their
chances are of succeeding?

00:49:26.280 --> 00:49:29.179
You've seen what the ray
guns have already done here.

00:49:29.180 --> 00:49:31.199
If they send out a fleet
of rocket ships armed

00:49:31.200 --> 00:49:34.819
with atomic weapons like those
or perhaps even larger ones

00:49:34.820 --> 00:49:36.890
it would be difficult to
hold out against them.

00:49:37.750 --> 00:49:38.929
Perhaps our best move would be

00:49:38.930 --> 00:49:40.769
to attempt an attack on the Moon.

00:49:40.770 --> 00:49:42.669
We'd be at a terrific disadvantage.

00:49:42.670 --> 00:49:44.269
I don't even see how we could land ships

00:49:44.270 --> 00:49:45.479
there in face of their ray guns.

00:49:45.480 --> 00:49:47.939
But we just can't sit here
and wait to be attacked.

00:49:47.940 --> 00:49:48.940
No, of course not.

00:49:49.830 --> 00:49:52.529
Retik the Ruler told me
they plan to attack after

00:49:52.530 --> 00:49:55.239
their saboteurs here have
accomplished their mission.

00:49:55.240 --> 00:49:57.559
If we could round up the gang operating here

00:49:57.560 --> 00:49:59.079
we may stave off the attack until

00:49:59.080 --> 00:50:01.369
we are better prepared to meet it.

00:50:01.370 --> 00:50:03.620
Yes that's certainly the first thing to do.

00:50:04.700 --> 00:50:06.609
You know some of the saboteurs don't you?

00:50:06.610 --> 00:50:08.539
Yes, well that is by sight.

00:50:08.540 --> 00:50:10.849
And my flying suit gives
me a considerable advantage

00:50:10.850 --> 00:50:11.740
in running them down.

00:50:11.740 --> 00:50:12.573
Right.

00:50:12.574 --> 00:50:14.509
I'll have you notified whenever
there's another attack.

00:50:14.510 --> 00:50:17.929
In the meantime we'll put every
available man on this case.

00:50:17.930 --> 00:50:19.380
Goodbye Cody.
-Goodbye sir.

00:50:20.838 --> 00:50:24.088
(light dramatic music)

00:50:29.100 --> 00:50:32.479
I'll have this ray gun
finished in a short time now

00:50:32.480 --> 00:50:35.480
so you'd better arrange to get
another truck to mount it in.

00:50:36.500 --> 00:50:38.570
Okay, but I'll need some more money.

00:50:39.740 --> 00:50:41.309
You'll have to sell some
more of those jewels

00:50:41.310 --> 00:50:42.860
you brought down from the moon.

00:50:43.760 --> 00:50:44.869
I've only a few of them left

00:50:44.870 --> 00:50:46.820
and I must keep those for an emergency.

00:50:47.680 --> 00:50:49.369
It will be necessary for you to take

00:50:49.370 --> 00:50:51.110
up your career of bank robbery.

00:50:52.210 --> 00:50:53.819
Not me.

00:50:53.820 --> 00:50:55.909
I'm already on parole for that.

00:50:55.910 --> 00:50:58.219
I know but you would be wise

00:50:58.220 --> 00:51:01.209
to continue to obey my orders.

00:51:01.210 --> 00:51:02.899
Your more recent activities would be

00:51:02.900 --> 00:51:05.130
of extreme interest to the authorities.

00:51:11.990 --> 00:51:14.099
Will you need someone to help you?

00:51:14.100 --> 00:51:16.470
Yeah, but they'll have to do the dirty work.

00:51:17.605 --> 00:51:19.319
Of course I'll go along to check on them.

00:51:19.320 --> 00:51:22.129
Very well, make your arrangements at once.

00:51:22.130 --> 00:51:23.549
Select a bank which is located

00:51:23.550 --> 00:51:25.560
in a not too heavily patrolled area.

00:51:28.150 --> 00:51:31.548
(light dramatic music)

00:51:31.549 --> 00:51:34.216
(alarm ringing)

00:51:39.480 --> 00:51:42.360
Something went wrong.

00:51:45.781 --> 00:51:46.614
Here they come.

00:51:47.986 --> 00:51:50.307
(banging)

00:51:50.308 --> 00:51:53.141
(engine rumbling)

00:51:59.610 --> 00:52:01.169
After that car.

00:52:01.170 --> 00:52:02.003
Step on it!

00:52:07.520 --> 00:52:08.539
(banging)

00:52:08.540 --> 00:52:10.890
We oughta lose 'em now,
we're out of traffic.

00:52:30.952 --> 00:52:33.202
(crashing)

00:52:41.570 --> 00:52:43.809
But we must have more money.

00:52:43.810 --> 00:52:45.260
You've got to get it somehow.

00:52:46.180 --> 00:52:47.929
Not by any more bank jobs.

00:52:47.930 --> 00:52:49.580
I'm too hot in that business now.

00:52:50.459 --> 00:52:52.459
We'll have to figure out something else.

00:52:55.650 --> 00:52:58.530
I'll radio the moon,
perhaps Retik can advise us.

00:53:03.140 --> 00:53:04.975
Krog calling Retik.

00:53:04.976 --> 00:53:08.059
(light spooky music)

00:53:13.022 --> 00:53:14.605
Krog calling Retik.

00:53:16.610 --> 00:53:17.910
Krog calling Retik.

00:53:21.140 --> 00:53:22.309
Come in, Krog.

00:53:22.310 --> 00:53:24.009
I have to report that our scheme

00:53:24.010 --> 00:53:27.199
for obtaining money was a
failure Your Excellency.

00:53:27.200 --> 00:53:30.339
Can you suggest some plan
that might be more successful?

00:53:30.340 --> 00:53:31.650
I think I can.

00:53:32.520 --> 00:53:34.489
From what I hear of activities on Earth

00:53:34.490 --> 00:53:36.239
kidnapping important persons and holding

00:53:36.240 --> 00:53:39.459
them for ransom has
proved highly profitable.

00:53:39.460 --> 00:53:41.959
Commando Cody who threw
his rocket ship to the moon

00:53:41.960 --> 00:53:45.179
is very valuable to the defense
organization of his country.

00:53:45.180 --> 00:53:47.139
I suggest you select him.

00:53:47.140 --> 00:53:48.679
An excellent idea.

00:53:48.680 --> 00:53:50.180
We shall carry it out at once.

00:53:51.570 --> 00:53:52.959
It'll be a rough deal,

00:53:52.960 --> 00:53:55.060
but a lot safer than robbing another bank.

00:53:55.900 --> 00:53:56.733
Of course.

00:53:57.910 --> 00:54:01.300
Commando Cody should be
worth at least $100,000.

00:54:02.760 --> 00:54:03.760
Shall we bring him here?

00:54:03.761 --> 00:54:04.989
No.

00:54:04.990 --> 00:54:06.820
Hire a plane and take him to...

00:54:07.660 --> 00:54:11.243
(light instrumental music)

00:54:15.066 --> 00:54:17.233
(tapping)

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:30.833
Where's Cody?

00:54:32.050 --> 00:54:33.130
[Ted] Right over there.

00:54:34.520 --> 00:54:37.270
(dramatic music)

00:54:44.531 --> 00:54:46.781
(thudding)

00:54:52.552 --> 00:54:54.969
(clattering)

00:54:56.281 --> 00:54:58.531
(grunting)

00:55:52.065 --> 00:55:54.119
Now will you tell us where Cody is?

00:55:54.120 --> 00:55:55.369
I don't know.

00:55:55.370 --> 00:55:58.629
Why don't we grab her
and use her to trap Cody?

00:55:58.630 --> 00:55:59.480
That's an idea.

00:56:00.680 --> 00:56:01.630
On your way sister.

00:56:04.130 --> 00:56:04.963
Wait a minute.

00:56:11.205 --> 00:56:14.455
(light dramatic music)

00:56:39.700 --> 00:56:40.533
What happened?

00:56:40.533 --> 00:56:41.460
Those same two men who wrecked

00:56:41.461 --> 00:56:43.359
the ray gun, they came after you.

00:56:43.360 --> 00:56:44.250
Where's Joan?

00:56:44.251 --> 00:56:45.990
I don't know, maybe they took her with them.

00:56:47.370 --> 00:56:48.389
Two men and a woman drove away

00:56:48.390 --> 00:56:50.019
from here just as I came in.

00:56:50.020 --> 00:56:51.489
They were too far away to be recognized

00:56:51.490 --> 00:56:52.840
but it must have been them.

00:56:56.780 --> 00:56:58.289
Police headquarters.

00:56:58.290 --> 00:57:03.290
(engines buzzing) (dramatic music)

00:57:18.026 --> 00:57:20.943
(tires screeching)

00:57:22.950 --> 00:57:24.599
Okay I'll tell him.

00:57:24.600 --> 00:57:26.239
The police found out that
the car went to the Eastside.

00:57:26.240 --> 00:57:28.819
Airport and a man took off
with Joan in a trotted plane.

00:57:28.820 --> 00:57:30.189
They left just a few minutes ago.

00:57:30.190 --> 00:57:32.423
If I'm lucky I can catch them.

00:57:43.791 --> 00:57:48.399
(blasting) (dramatic music)

00:57:48.400 --> 00:57:51.233
(engine rattling)

00:58:20.739 --> 00:58:22.569
Don't get excited, sister.

00:58:22.570 --> 00:58:23.927
I'll take care of him.

00:58:29.399 --> 00:58:31.566
(banging)

00:58:51.823 --> 00:58:54.073
(clicking)

00:59:07.823 --> 00:59:10.573
(dramatic music)

00:59:56.438 --> 00:59:58.605
He wrecked the controls.

01:00:08.486 --> 01:00:09.840
(booming)

01:00:09.841 --> 01:00:12.591
(dramatic music)

01:00:23.576 --> 01:00:26.326
(dramatic music)

01:01:48.721 --> 01:01:51.554
(engine rumbling)

01:02:13.900 --> 01:02:16.067
He wrecked the controls.

01:02:19.400 --> 01:02:22.150
[Cody] Get into that parachute.

01:02:41.215 --> 01:02:43.382
(booming)

01:03:09.830 --> 01:03:10.959
What became of that man?

01:03:10.960 --> 01:03:12.619
[Cody] He must have
landed somewhere near here.

01:03:12.620 --> 01:03:14.609
If you're sure you're all
right, I'll look for him.

01:03:14.610 --> 01:03:16.979
Oh, of course I am I'll
walk over to the road.

01:03:16.980 --> 01:03:17.813
[Cody] Okay.

01:03:23.567 --> 01:03:28.567
(blasting) (dramatic music)

01:03:53.207 --> 01:03:54.899
How about a ride to town mister?

01:03:54.900 --> 01:03:56.567
Well sure, hop in.

01:04:08.549 --> 01:04:10.799
(blasting)

01:04:24.369 --> 01:04:26.700
Man in a flying suit chasing us, step on it.

01:04:26.701 --> 01:04:28.319
Huh, are you crazy?

01:04:28.320 --> 01:04:30.023
Don't argue, step on it.

01:04:35.952 --> 01:04:38.119
(banging)

01:04:59.610 --> 01:05:00.460
That stopped him.

01:05:01.600 --> 01:05:02.770
You keep going.

01:05:04.497 --> 01:05:06.747
(rustling)

01:05:24.076 --> 01:05:25.476
I must report to the Moon.

01:05:31.080 --> 01:05:32.100
Krog calling Retik.

01:05:39.880 --> 01:05:40.830
Krog calling Retik.

01:05:43.730 --> 01:05:44.840
Krog calling Retik.

01:05:50.370 --> 01:05:51.509
Come in Krog.

01:05:51.510 --> 01:05:54.199
I have to report another
failure, Your Excellency.

01:05:54.200 --> 01:05:56.089
We were unable to capture Commando Cody

01:05:56.090 --> 01:05:57.619
and hold him for ransom.

01:05:57.620 --> 01:05:59.339
You still have no funds.

01:05:59.340 --> 01:06:00.270
No, sir.

01:06:00.271 --> 01:06:02.069
And until we can get a ray gun into action

01:06:02.070 --> 01:06:03.689
again we are unable to continue our

01:06:03.690 --> 01:06:06.019
campaign against Earth's defenses.

01:06:06.020 --> 01:06:07.939
Listen carefully Krog,

01:06:07.940 --> 01:06:11.149
I cannot have my preparations
for invading the earth

01:06:11.150 --> 01:06:13.029
delayed by such a minor detail as

01:06:13.030 --> 01:06:15.049
obtaining a small amount of money.

01:06:15.050 --> 01:06:17.129
If the men you now have cannot accomplish

01:06:17.130 --> 01:06:19.009
this simple mission then hire

01:06:19.010 --> 01:06:21.199
someone who can produce results.

01:06:21.200 --> 01:06:22.739
This is an order!

01:06:22.740 --> 01:06:24.340
I understand, Your Excellency.

01:06:31.850 --> 01:06:32.683
You heard.

01:06:33.870 --> 01:06:35.719
It's up to you to decide
whether you can still

01:06:35.720 --> 01:06:37.530
be useful to us or...

01:06:39.230 --> 01:06:40.680
We'll figure something out.

01:06:42.800 --> 01:06:44.289
Remember that payroll job Duke

01:06:44.290 --> 01:06:46.179
was trying to get you in on?

01:06:46.180 --> 01:06:48.030
Maybe he'll still go through with it.

01:06:49.790 --> 01:06:50.623
Well?

01:06:51.900 --> 01:06:53.979
It's risky but it might work.

01:06:53.980 --> 01:06:56.439
It's the Western Wholesale Supply Company.

01:06:56.440 --> 01:06:57.410
They keep their payroll in

01:06:57.411 --> 01:06:59.819
the office safe every Friday night.

01:06:59.820 --> 01:07:02.520
There's a man in the office
who knows the combination.

01:07:04.220 --> 01:07:05.911
(alarm ringing)

01:07:05.912 --> 01:07:08.662
(dramatic music)

01:07:18.509 --> 01:07:20.435
(whistle blowing)

01:07:20.436 --> 01:07:25.436
There's a cop, get going.

01:07:25.728 --> 01:07:27.895
(banging)

01:07:34.232 --> 01:07:35.463
Hold up men in a black sedan.

01:07:35.464 --> 01:07:39.388
They took the turn to the right.

01:07:39.389 --> 01:07:41.207
(dramatic music)

01:07:41.208 --> 01:07:44.125
(tires screeching)

01:08:19.661 --> 01:08:21.146
(banging)

01:08:21.147 --> 01:08:23.099
They're gettin' closer.

01:08:23.100 --> 01:08:24.659
We can't get caught with the payroll on us.

01:08:24.660 --> 01:08:27.010
Watch where I throw it,
we'll pick it up later.

01:08:43.093 --> 01:08:45.510
(clattering)

01:09:00.800 --> 01:09:02.050
We finally got a break.

01:09:03.180 --> 01:09:04.629
They called me down to the jail hospital

01:09:04.630 --> 01:09:06.609
to see if I could identify a prisoner

01:09:06.610 --> 01:09:08.089
and he turned out to be one of those two

01:09:08.090 --> 01:09:09.579
who've been making all the trouble for us.

01:09:09.580 --> 01:09:10.869
Well how did they catch him?

01:09:10.870 --> 01:09:13.249
Well he and another man
staged a payroll robbery.

01:09:13.250 --> 01:09:15.469
The police went after
them and the car crashed.

01:09:15.470 --> 01:09:16.749
The other man was killed but her pal

01:09:16.750 --> 01:09:18.219
was only banged up a little.

01:09:18.220 --> 01:09:20.149
What did you find out about him?

01:09:20.150 --> 01:09:22.169
His name's Graber, he's an ex-convict

01:09:22.170 --> 01:09:24.169
out on parole from a bank robbery sentence.

01:09:24.170 --> 01:09:25.239
Well what about his connection

01:09:25.240 --> 01:09:26.979
with the invaders from the moon?

01:09:26.980 --> 01:09:29.039
I haven't had a chance to find out yet.

01:09:29.040 --> 01:09:31.119
There were too many people
around the jail hospital

01:09:31.120 --> 01:09:33.199
so Henderson asked me not
to question him there.

01:09:33.200 --> 01:09:34.849
We might be overheard.

01:09:34.850 --> 01:09:37.029
But aren't they going to
try to find out something?

01:09:37.030 --> 01:09:37.930
Yes.

01:09:37.931 --> 01:09:39.159
They're going to move him under guard

01:09:39.160 --> 01:09:41.499
to a private sanitarium
where we can question

01:09:41.500 --> 01:09:43.869
him without any danger
of the story leaking out

01:09:43.870 --> 01:09:45.919
and throwing the whole country into a panic.

01:09:45.920 --> 01:09:46.969
When will that be?

01:09:46.970 --> 01:09:48.349
Probably this afternoon.

01:09:48.350 --> 01:09:49.729
Henderson is going to let me know as soon as

01:09:49.730 --> 01:09:51.819
they make arrangements for
having him transferred.

01:09:51.820 --> 01:09:53.109
I'd like you to go with me Ted.

01:09:53.110 --> 01:09:54.084
Sure.

01:09:54.085 --> 01:09:57.334
(light dramatic music)

01:09:58.380 --> 01:10:00.049
I got some news about Graber.

01:10:00.050 --> 01:10:02.299
A friend of mine's a
trustee in the jail hospital

01:10:02.300 --> 01:10:03.719
and he tipped me off they're moving Graber

01:10:03.720 --> 01:10:05.519
out in an ambulance this afternoon.

01:10:05.520 --> 01:10:07.099
Is there anything we can do about it?

01:10:07.100 --> 01:10:09.139
Yeah I got it all figured out.

01:10:09.140 --> 01:10:10.579
Now my friend told me which road

01:10:10.580 --> 01:10:12.411
the ambulance is taking and I'll...

01:10:12.412 --> 01:10:15.662
(light dramatic music)

01:10:25.220 --> 01:10:28.137
(tires screeching)

01:10:37.860 --> 01:10:39.450
Start walking across country.

01:10:40.500 --> 01:10:41.333
Go on!

01:10:58.383 --> 01:10:59.290
What about the driver?

01:10:59.291 --> 01:11:00.469
I sent him hiking.

01:11:00.470 --> 01:11:01.360
You should have slugged him.

01:11:01.360 --> 01:11:02.240
As soon as he gets to a phone

01:11:02.241 --> 01:11:03.379
he'll have the cops on our trial.

01:11:03.380 --> 01:11:04.399
Nah, it's okay.

01:11:04.400 --> 01:11:06.769
There's a car parked a few miles
up the road to pick you up.

01:11:06.770 --> 01:11:07.620
Okay, let's go.

01:11:10.297 --> 01:11:13.047
(dramatic music)

01:11:28.387 --> 01:11:31.220
(engine rumbling)

01:11:37.710 --> 01:11:39.429
It's about time you got here,

01:11:39.430 --> 01:11:41.159
the cops are after you already.

01:11:41.160 --> 01:11:42.050
What?

01:11:42.051 --> 01:11:44.210
Yeah it's coming over the radio right now.

01:11:48.060 --> 01:11:50.509
[Dispatch] Calling all
cars, calling all cars.

01:11:50.510 --> 01:11:52.259
The stolen ambulance was last reported

01:11:52.260 --> 01:11:55.039
turning onto the east end
of Harrison Canyon Highway.

01:11:55.040 --> 01:11:57.199
I told ya you should
have slugged that driver.

01:11:57.200 --> 01:11:59.059
[Dispatch] Calling police headquarters,

01:11:59.060 --> 01:12:01.079
calling police headquarters.

01:12:01.080 --> 01:12:02.249
It's Cody.

01:12:02.250 --> 01:12:03.889
[Dispatch] Police headquarters, come in.

01:12:03.890 --> 01:12:05.559
[Cody] This is Commando Cody, I picked up

01:12:05.560 --> 01:12:07.169
your broadcast and I'm just turning in

01:12:07.170 --> 01:12:08.879
to the west end of Harrison Canyon now.

01:12:08.880 --> 01:12:11.130
If I meet the ambulance
I'll stop it for you.

01:12:12.100 --> 01:12:14.199
[Dispatch] We'll get some
men up there soon as we can.

01:12:14.200 --> 01:12:15.339
That's a bad break.

01:12:15.340 --> 01:12:16.719
What's he doing out here?

01:12:16.720 --> 01:12:18.819
Probably on his way to third degree me.

01:12:18.820 --> 01:12:20.489
I'll go back to town with you Sam.

01:12:20.490 --> 01:12:22.629
You keep going with the
ambulance until you can ditch it.

01:12:22.630 --> 01:12:24.569
If you meet Cody first smash him.

01:12:24.570 --> 01:12:25.403
Right!

01:12:28.623 --> 01:12:31.456
(engine rumbling)

01:12:48.360 --> 01:12:50.519
Do you think we'll meet them on the road?

01:12:50.520 --> 01:12:51.820
We got a good chance to.

01:13:07.296 --> 01:13:10.296
(suspenseful music)

01:13:21.490 --> 01:13:22.323
There it is!

01:13:26.521 --> 01:13:27.771
It's gonna crash into us!

01:13:29.425 --> 01:13:31.675
(crashing)

01:13:32.794 --> 01:13:35.544
(dramatic music)

01:13:48.279 --> 01:13:51.029
(dramatic music)

01:15:17.701 --> 01:15:20.020
Do you think we'll meet them on the road?

01:15:20.021 --> 01:15:21.316
We've got a good chance to.

01:15:23.092 --> 01:15:25.842
(dramatic music)

01:15:44.577 --> 01:15:45.744
There it is!

01:15:49.566 --> 01:15:51.065
It's gonna crash into us!

01:15:51.066 --> 01:15:51.966
[Cody] Bail out!

01:15:56.756 --> 01:15:59.006
(crashing)

01:16:07.138 --> 01:16:09.638
(light music)

01:16:12.256 --> 01:16:13.306
Here's the payroll.

01:16:14.312 --> 01:16:15.735
We found it right where it was thrown.

01:16:15.736 --> 01:16:16.965
Splendid.

01:16:16.966 --> 01:16:18.716
Now we can...
-Retik calling Krog.

01:16:20.636 --> 01:16:21.686
Retik calling Krog.

01:16:29.856 --> 01:16:31.325
Yes, Your Excellency?

01:16:31.326 --> 01:16:33.365
I was just about to call
you to report that we are

01:16:33.366 --> 01:16:35.935
about to put our ray gun
into operation again.

01:16:35.936 --> 01:16:38.575
I have another mission for you first.

01:16:38.576 --> 01:16:41.775
Do you have an atomic bomb strong enough to

01:16:41.776 --> 01:16:44.885
start a volcanic eruption
in the Mount Aldo Crater?

01:16:44.886 --> 01:16:46.665
Yes but an eruption in that mountainous

01:16:46.666 --> 01:16:48.765
area would do very little damage.

01:16:48.766 --> 01:16:51.995
On the contrary, it will
do a great deal of damage.

01:16:51.996 --> 01:16:55.185
The present atmospheric
conditions on Earth indicate

01:16:55.186 --> 01:16:57.875
that the eruption would
cause torrential rains

01:16:57.876 --> 01:16:59.765
and the resulting floods should seriously

01:16:59.766 --> 01:17:02.645
disrupt transportation and defense measures.

01:17:02.646 --> 01:17:03.479
Excellent idea.

01:17:03.480 --> 01:17:05.105
We shall carry it out at once.

01:17:05.106 --> 01:17:06.155
Very well.

01:17:06.156 --> 01:17:09.225
Then start an intensified
campaign with the ray gun.

01:17:09.226 --> 01:17:12.155
Earth's defenses must be
completely broken down

01:17:12.156 --> 01:17:14.405
before we can risk an
invasion from the moon.

01:17:14.406 --> 01:17:15.536
Yes Your Excellency.

01:17:20.913 --> 01:17:24.085
You heard the orders,
charter a plane and drop one

01:17:24.086 --> 01:17:26.655
of our atomic bombs into the outer crater.

01:17:26.656 --> 01:17:28.475
Nature will do the rest.

01:17:28.476 --> 01:17:29.875
Okay, when do we do it?

01:17:29.876 --> 01:17:31.455
At once.

01:17:31.456 --> 01:17:32.656
I will get you the bomb.

01:17:36.941 --> 01:17:40.441
(light suspenseful music)

01:17:43.090 --> 01:17:48.090
(rumbling) (dramatic music)

01:18:08.422 --> 01:18:09.672
Here it goes.

01:18:12.153 --> 01:18:14.320
(booming)

01:19:09.346 --> 01:19:11.295
If the moon men did start that eruption

01:19:11.296 --> 01:19:13.305
they certainly got results.

01:19:13.306 --> 01:19:15.155
Well somebody must have started it.

01:19:15.156 --> 01:19:16.825
That volcano has been dead for years.

01:19:16.826 --> 01:19:19.345
Took quite a blast to get it going again.

01:19:19.346 --> 01:19:21.135
An atomic bomb dropped from a plane

01:19:21.136 --> 01:19:22.985
would seem to be the only answer.

01:19:22.986 --> 01:19:25.117
You know Commando Cody thinks that maybe...

01:19:25.118 --> 01:19:27.785
(door clicking)

01:19:30.176 --> 01:19:31.009
How'd you make out?

01:19:31.009 --> 01:19:31.936
I think we're on the right track.

01:19:31.937 --> 01:19:34.055
The second airport I checked had chartered

01:19:34.056 --> 01:19:35.735
the plane on the day of the eruption to two

01:19:35.736 --> 01:19:38.525
men answering the description
of Graber and his pal.

01:19:38.526 --> 01:19:39.359
Then we're right.

01:19:39.360 --> 01:19:40.745
They're the ones who bombed the volcano.

01:19:40.746 --> 01:19:41.579
Looks like it.

01:19:41.580 --> 01:19:43.135
Yes but that doesn't help us catch them.

01:19:43.136 --> 01:19:44.395
Couldn't you get a line on them?

01:19:44.396 --> 01:19:46.305
The names and addresses
they gave were phony,

01:19:46.306 --> 01:19:47.935
but I did get one break.

01:19:47.936 --> 01:19:49.375
The airport manager borrowed these matches

01:19:49.376 --> 01:19:51.445
from Graber and forgot to give them back.

01:19:51.446 --> 01:19:52.595
Al's Cafe.

01:19:52.596 --> 01:19:53.705
That might do us some good.

01:19:53.706 --> 01:19:55.275
It at least means they've been there

01:19:55.276 --> 01:19:57.385
and if we're lucky they
might be regular customers.

01:19:57.386 --> 01:19:58.785
So let's go and look the joint over.

01:19:58.786 --> 01:20:00.285
Right.

01:20:00.286 --> 01:20:02.196
If we hear anything Joan,
we'll give you a call.

01:20:09.506 --> 01:20:11.235
Yeah I know the guys you mean.

01:20:11.236 --> 01:20:12.605
They come in here pretty often

01:20:12.606 --> 01:20:14.975
but I don't know their
names or anything about 'em.

01:20:14.976 --> 01:20:16.866
Well, if they show up I wish you'd call me.

01:20:18.586 --> 01:20:19.685
Oh, sure.

01:20:19.686 --> 01:20:20.990
I sure will, Mr. Cody.

01:20:20.991 --> 01:20:25.278
Thanks.

01:20:25.279 --> 01:20:27.094
(dramatic music)

01:20:27.095 --> 01:20:29.345
(thudding)

01:20:30.495 --> 01:20:32.912
(clattering)

01:20:51.434 --> 01:20:53.851
(shattering)

01:20:57.557 --> 01:20:59.807
(grunting)

01:21:12.909 --> 01:21:15.242
Drop it or I'll drill him.

01:21:16.473 --> 01:21:17.685
If you or the cops try to follow us

01:21:17.686 --> 01:21:18.986
I'll give it to him quick.

01:21:48.166 --> 01:21:50.445
They took your pal Mr. Cody.

01:21:50.446 --> 01:21:51.775
You gonna call the cops?

01:21:51.776 --> 01:21:53.225
I don't dare to.

01:21:53.226 --> 01:21:54.276
They'd kill him sure.

01:22:19.158 --> 01:22:24.158
(banging) (dramatic music)

01:22:24.440 --> 01:22:27.357
(tires screeching)

01:22:39.222 --> 01:22:40.375
[Daly] We'll never find him down there.

01:22:40.376 --> 01:22:41.209
You're right.

01:22:41.210 --> 01:22:42.355
And as soon as he can get to a phone

01:22:42.356 --> 01:22:44.006
he'll have the cops on our trail.

01:22:45.496 --> 01:22:47.765
The road to Clark Mountain is just up ahead.

01:22:47.766 --> 01:22:50.526
We'll hide out there until
Krog can send us another car.

01:23:00.816 --> 01:23:01.865
Calling Krog.

01:23:01.866 --> 01:23:03.105
Calling Krog.

01:23:03.106 --> 01:23:04.325
[Krog] Come in, Graber.

01:23:04.326 --> 01:23:06.445
We just had a run-in with Cody again.

01:23:06.446 --> 01:23:07.845
Our car is hot.

01:23:07.846 --> 01:23:09.865
We'll have to have another one.

01:23:09.866 --> 01:23:11.345
[Krog] Where are you?

01:23:11.346 --> 01:23:13.015
We're heading up to Clark Mountain.

01:23:13.016 --> 01:23:15.295
We'll stop before we get
to the top and wait there.

01:23:15.296 --> 01:23:16.615
Very well I'll have another car out

01:23:16.616 --> 01:23:17.916
there as soon as possible.

01:23:21.651 --> 01:23:24.401
(dramatic music)

01:23:31.236 --> 01:23:32.725
What do you think they'll do to him?

01:23:32.726 --> 01:23:33.905
Oh it's hard to tell.

01:23:33.906 --> 01:23:35.149
They'll certainly hold him until they...

01:23:35.150 --> 01:23:36.875
(phone ringing)

01:23:36.876 --> 01:23:38.345
Cody Laboratory.

01:23:38.346 --> 01:23:40.035
Ted, where are you!

01:23:40.036 --> 01:23:42.245
In a gas station on Highway 17.

01:23:42.246 --> 01:23:44.325
I jumped out of the car
and gave them the slip.

01:23:44.326 --> 01:23:45.256
Good work.

01:23:45.257 --> 01:23:46.375
Now we can go after them.

01:23:46.376 --> 01:23:47.595
Where are they heading?

01:23:47.596 --> 01:23:49.505
They were going up the Clark Mountain road.

01:23:49.506 --> 01:23:51.455
I'll use the rocket
suit and try to find them.

01:23:51.456 --> 01:23:52.289
Okay.

01:23:52.290 --> 01:23:54.376
Don't worry about me I'll
come right back to town.

01:23:58.296 --> 01:23:59.755
Phone the police and
tell the block to highway

01:23:59.756 --> 01:24:00.886
on the other side of the mountain.

01:24:00.887 --> 01:24:04.526
Right.

01:24:06.116 --> 01:24:07.116
Police headquarters.

01:24:11.397 --> 01:24:13.268
(dramatic music)

01:24:13.269 --> 01:24:15.519
(blasting)

01:24:40.126 --> 01:24:40.959
Hey, Daly.

01:24:42.196 --> 01:24:43.029
Quit worrying.

01:24:44.306 --> 01:24:46.066
Car can't get here for a while yet.

01:24:51.280 --> 01:24:54.030
(dramatic music)

01:25:33.565 --> 01:25:35.315
Hey, hey it's Cody.

01:25:37.833 --> 01:25:38.848
(banging)

01:25:38.849 --> 01:25:41.599
(dramatic music)

01:26:00.549 --> 01:26:02.065
It's time to get out of here.

01:26:02.066 --> 01:26:03.343
Follow me, keep low.

01:26:09.399 --> 01:26:12.149
(dramatic music)

01:26:35.221 --> 01:26:36.715
When Cody gets here give yourself up.

01:26:36.716 --> 01:26:38.175
Try not to get too close to him.

01:26:38.176 --> 01:26:39.755
-But look...
-Don't argue,

01:26:39.756 --> 01:26:41.183
do what I tell ya.

01:26:43.154 --> 01:26:46.154
(suspenseful music)

01:26:47.536 --> 01:26:49.203
[Cody] Don't move.

01:26:52.914 --> 01:26:55.039
Drop your gun.

01:26:55.040 --> 01:26:56.555
Where's Graber?

01:26:56.556 --> 01:26:58.369
(thudding)

01:26:58.370 --> 01:27:01.120
(dramatic music)

01:27:10.488 --> 01:27:13.238
(dramatic music)

01:28:51.607 --> 01:28:53.365
When Cody gets here give yourself up.

01:28:53.366 --> 01:28:54.815
Try not to get too close to him.

01:28:54.816 --> 01:28:56.385
-But look...
-Don't argue,

01:28:56.386 --> 01:28:57.286
do what I tell ya.

01:29:04.127 --> 01:29:05.210
Don't move.

01:29:09.583 --> 01:29:11.465
Drop your gun.

01:29:11.466 --> 01:29:13.221
Where's Graber?

01:29:13.222 --> 01:29:18.222
(thudding) (dramatic music)

01:29:21.000 --> 01:29:23.333
(whooshing)

01:29:32.486 --> 01:29:34.105
I got the flying suit under control just

01:29:34.106 --> 01:29:36.256
before I crashed but I'd lost my gun.

01:29:37.142 --> 01:29:38.036
When I tried to look for Graber

01:29:38.037 --> 01:29:39.525
and his pal they had disappeared.

01:29:39.526 --> 01:29:41.825
They'd must have taken
over the hills on foot.

01:29:41.826 --> 01:29:43.305
So where are we now?

01:29:43.306 --> 01:29:45.055
About back where we started.

01:29:45.056 --> 01:29:46.355
Except that we do know that Graber's

01:29:46.356 --> 01:29:48.035
been hanging out at Al's Cafe.

01:29:48.036 --> 01:29:50.555
They'll probably never show up there again.

01:29:50.556 --> 01:29:53.175
But I might find somebody
around there who knows them.

01:29:53.176 --> 01:29:55.175
Anyway I'm going to give it a try.

01:29:55.176 --> 01:29:56.176
I'll call you later.

01:30:02.896 --> 01:30:05.175
Sure I've seen him around
here and talked to him

01:30:05.176 --> 01:30:08.015
a few times but I don't
know anything about him.

01:30:08.016 --> 01:30:09.435
What'd you talk to him about?

01:30:09.436 --> 01:30:11.605
Well I'm a mechanic and
the last time he asked me

01:30:11.606 --> 01:30:13.355
to do some work on a truck motor for him

01:30:13.356 --> 01:30:16.555
I couldn't handle the
job so yesterday it was,

01:30:16.556 --> 01:30:18.995
I told him to try Benson's
over on the south side of town

01:30:18.996 --> 01:30:21.796
but I don't know whether they
ever went over there or not.

01:30:22.846 --> 01:30:23.679
I'll check up on that.

01:30:23.680 --> 01:30:25.685
Do you know Benson's address?

01:30:25.686 --> 01:30:28.235
It's on Central between 14th and 15th.

01:30:28.236 --> 01:30:29.486
South side of the street.

01:30:32.116 --> 01:30:33.255
Good, thanks.

01:30:33.256 --> 01:30:34.246
I'll let you know if they ever turn

01:30:34.247 --> 01:30:35.525
up here again Mr. Cody.

01:30:35.526 --> 01:30:36.626
Good, see you later.

01:30:37.718 --> 01:30:40.801
(light spooky music)

01:30:48.816 --> 01:30:52.939
Krog calling Retik.

01:30:55.325 --> 01:30:56.586
Krog calling Retik.

01:31:03.969 --> 01:31:04.866
Come in, Krog.

01:31:04.867 --> 01:31:06.415
We have the new ray gun ready to mount in

01:31:06.416 --> 01:31:09.036
a well camouflaged truck Your Excellency.

01:31:09.037 --> 01:31:11.035
And are prepared to renew our campaign.

01:31:11.036 --> 01:31:11.869
Good.

01:31:11.870 --> 01:31:13.395
What are your first objectives?

01:31:13.396 --> 01:31:14.875
Since the authorities here learned of

01:31:14.876 --> 01:31:17.185
your planned invasion from the moon,

01:31:17.186 --> 01:31:19.715
there have been heavy troop
movements in this area.

01:31:19.716 --> 01:31:22.965
We plan to concentrate on
destroying troop trains.

01:31:22.966 --> 01:31:23.799
Very well.

01:31:23.800 --> 01:31:25.515
Work as fast as possible.

01:31:25.516 --> 01:31:28.225
We must have Earth's defenses
completely disorganized

01:31:28.226 --> 01:31:30.855
before we start our invasion from the moon.

01:31:30.856 --> 01:31:32.086
Yes, Your Excellency.

01:31:39.553 --> 01:31:40.765
Is everything ready?

01:31:40.766 --> 01:31:43.076
Yes, we can pick up the truck and get going.

01:31:44.716 --> 01:31:46.025
Here are the timetables.

01:31:46.026 --> 01:31:48.835
The map with the best
points of attack indicated.

01:31:48.836 --> 01:31:51.585
Cover as many of them as you can today.

01:31:51.586 --> 01:31:52.419
Right.

01:31:54.032 --> 01:31:56.685
(light dramatic music)

01:31:56.686 --> 01:31:59.665
No, I don't remember anyone
answering that description

01:31:59.666 --> 01:32:01.225
but of course we run a
lot of jobs through here

01:32:01.226 --> 01:32:02.876
and I don't know all the drivers.

01:32:03.716 --> 01:32:06.025
How about these trucks that are in here now?

01:32:06.026 --> 01:32:07.735
Well this one and this one are

01:32:07.736 --> 01:32:09.865
a couple of my regular customers.

01:32:09.866 --> 01:32:12.125
That was a cross-country
job it came in last night

01:32:12.126 --> 01:32:13.835
for an ignition check.

01:32:13.836 --> 01:32:15.215
I didn't see who the driver was,

01:32:15.216 --> 01:32:16.515
the night man took care of it.

01:32:16.516 --> 01:32:17.456
Okay if I look it over?

01:32:17.456 --> 01:32:18.356
Sure, go ahead.

01:32:27.984 --> 01:32:30.770
(rattling)

01:32:30.771 --> 01:32:33.021
(clanking)

01:32:34.995 --> 01:32:36.615
Get away from that truck.

01:32:36.616 --> 01:32:37.885
Hey, what's going on?

01:32:37.886 --> 01:32:38.985
Frisk him.

01:32:38.986 --> 01:32:40.295
Stay out of this or you'll get hurt.

01:32:40.296 --> 01:32:42.385
Now look, I don't want any trouble in here.

01:32:42.386 --> 01:32:47.386
(dramatic music) (grunting)

01:32:52.285 --> 01:32:54.535
(thudding)

01:33:22.454 --> 01:33:24.871
(clattering)

01:33:47.750 --> 01:33:52.750
Let's roll.

01:34:00.202 --> 01:34:03.035
(engine rumbling)

01:34:17.596 --> 01:34:19.785
That truckload of radios was a phony.

01:34:19.786 --> 01:34:21.975
That whole back end was a fake door.

01:34:21.976 --> 01:34:24.385
I'm sure they're planning
and hiding something inside.

01:34:24.386 --> 01:34:25.845
Probably a ray gun.

01:34:25.846 --> 01:34:27.475
That's what I'm afraid of.

01:34:27.476 --> 01:34:30.165
They'll probably start
blasting again any time now.

01:34:30.166 --> 01:34:31.835
I've sent Ted out to the airport to stand

01:34:31.836 --> 01:34:34.075
by in a plane with some light bombs.

01:34:34.076 --> 01:34:35.665
Soon as we hear of any ray gun attacks

01:34:35.666 --> 01:34:37.675
I'll fly out and try to locate that truck

01:34:37.676 --> 01:34:39.634
and radio Ted to bomb it.

01:34:39.635 --> 01:34:41.935
(phone ringing)

01:34:41.936 --> 01:34:42.776
Cody Laboratory.

01:34:46.616 --> 01:34:48.565
All right, we'll be right out.

01:34:48.566 --> 01:34:49.845
They just blasted a troop train in the

01:34:49.846 --> 01:34:51.235
east end of Carson Valley.

01:34:51.236 --> 01:34:52.685
Radio Ted to take off and in a plane

01:34:52.686 --> 01:34:54.275
at once and fly around out there.

01:34:54.276 --> 01:34:56.455
I'll contact him as soon
as I spot the truck.

01:34:56.456 --> 01:34:57.289
Right away.

01:35:00.756 --> 01:35:02.355
Calling Ted Richards.

01:35:02.356 --> 01:35:03.516
Calling Ted Richards.

01:35:09.371 --> 01:35:12.121
(dramatic music)

01:35:51.472 --> 01:35:53.972
[Cody] Calling Ted Richards.

01:35:55.466 --> 01:35:57.335
Calling Ted Richards.

01:35:57.336 --> 01:35:58.785
This is Ted, come in.

01:35:58.786 --> 01:36:00.285
[Cody] I've spotted the truck.

01:36:00.286 --> 01:36:02.095
It's going along a dirt road just east

01:36:02.096 --> 01:36:03.355
of the end of the valley.

01:36:03.356 --> 01:36:04.475
I'll be right with you.

01:36:04.476 --> 01:36:09.476
[Cody] Okay, I'll keep them
in sight until you show up.

01:36:09.670 --> 01:36:12.420
(dramatic music)

01:36:37.496 --> 01:36:38.875
Cody's after us again!

01:36:38.876 --> 01:36:40.476
We'll stop him, use the rifle.

01:36:49.361 --> 01:36:51.528
(banging)

01:37:01.925 --> 01:37:03.420
Did you get him?

01:37:03.421 --> 01:37:05.685
No, but I scared him off.

01:37:05.686 --> 01:37:07.725
So he'll fly back and
tell the cops where we are?

01:37:07.726 --> 01:37:08.559
So what?

01:37:08.560 --> 01:37:11.706
By the time they get out
here we'll be long gone.

01:37:21.596 --> 01:37:22.796
[Cody] Ted, Ted.

01:37:24.116 --> 01:37:25.036
This is Ted.

01:37:25.037 --> 01:37:26.635
[Cody] You're headed the right direction,

01:37:26.636 --> 01:37:29.145
just keep going I'm coming aboard.

01:37:29.146 --> 01:37:29.979
Right.

01:37:32.406 --> 01:37:35.156
(dramatic music)

01:38:13.661 --> 01:38:14.494
What gives?

01:38:14.494 --> 01:38:15.409
The truck's just ahead.

01:38:15.410 --> 01:38:17.045
Fly over to that dirt road.

01:38:17.046 --> 01:38:17.879
Okay.

01:38:17.880 --> 01:38:19.019
[Cody] Where are the bombs?

01:38:19.020 --> 01:38:20.187
Right there.

01:38:28.554 --> 01:38:29.971
Right a little.

01:38:32.693 --> 01:38:34.465
That's good, just keep going.

01:38:34.466 --> 01:38:35.299
Okay.

01:38:40.692 --> 01:38:43.275
(booming)

01:38:43.276 --> 01:38:44.109
What was that?

01:38:47.336 --> 01:38:49.105
There's a plane up
there, he must of bombed us

01:38:49.106 --> 01:38:51.115
and looks like he's coming
back for another try.

01:38:51.116 --> 01:38:51.949
I'll stop.

01:38:51.950 --> 01:38:53.706
We'll give a blast with our ray gun.

01:38:55.189 --> 01:38:56.126
That was pretty close but drop

01:38:56.127 --> 01:38:57.589
down a little lower next time.

01:38:57.590 --> 01:39:02.590
Okay.

01:39:23.946 --> 01:39:24.996
Hey, they've stopped.

01:39:26.026 --> 01:39:27.925
Looks like they're aiming a gun at us.

01:39:27.926 --> 01:39:29.115
Dive on 'em, quick!

01:39:29.116 --> 01:39:29.949
Okay.

01:39:31.416 --> 01:39:34.525
(engine rumbling)

01:39:34.526 --> 01:39:37.423
Hurry it up, he's diving on us again!

01:39:37.424 --> 01:39:39.591
(booming)

01:39:41.350 --> 01:39:43.364
Ya missed!

01:39:43.365 --> 01:39:44.365
He came too quick.

01:39:44.366 --> 01:39:45.916
Turn the truck around, I'll
get another shot at him.

01:39:45.917 --> 01:39:50.917
Right!

01:40:03.563 --> 01:40:05.263
[Cody] They're getting
set for another shot at us.

01:40:05.264 --> 01:40:10.264
Get going.

01:40:21.715 --> 01:40:24.100
(booming)

01:40:24.101 --> 01:40:26.851
(dramatic music)

01:40:35.515 --> 01:40:38.265
(dramatic music)

01:42:01.216 --> 01:42:02.049
Ya missed!

01:42:03.116 --> 01:42:04.275
Came too quick.

01:42:04.276 --> 01:42:06.007
Turn the truck around, I
can get another shot at him.

01:42:06.008 --> 01:42:09.555
Right!

01:42:09.556 --> 01:42:12.389
(engine rumbling)

01:42:23.086 --> 01:42:24.939
[Cody] They're getting
set for another shot at us.

01:42:24.940 --> 01:42:28.339
Get going.

01:42:34.866 --> 01:42:36.359
Better bail out.

01:42:36.360 --> 01:42:41.360
Okay.

01:42:44.688 --> 01:42:47.007
(booming)

01:42:47.008 --> 01:42:49.758
(dramatic music)

01:43:19.509 --> 01:43:21.075
It's going to be a serious problem

01:43:21.076 --> 01:43:23.505
organizing any system of
defense against those ray guns.

01:43:23.506 --> 01:43:25.015
It's practically impossible

01:43:25.016 --> 01:43:26.505
unless we build ray guns of our own.

01:43:26.506 --> 01:43:27.885
We can't do that without lunarium

01:43:27.886 --> 01:43:29.395
as the base for the atom reaction.

01:43:29.396 --> 01:43:30.705
That's right.

01:43:30.706 --> 01:43:32.715
So if it meets with your
approval I'll make another trip

01:43:32.716 --> 01:43:35.685
to the moon and try to
get a supply of lunarium.

01:43:35.686 --> 01:43:36.835
Do you think you can do it?

01:43:36.836 --> 01:43:38.755
I'm not sure but it's worth trying.

01:43:38.756 --> 01:43:39.925
Anything is better than sitting here

01:43:39.926 --> 01:43:41.695
like tin ducks in a shooting gallery.

01:43:41.696 --> 01:43:43.865
I heartily agree and
if you're willing to make

01:43:43.866 --> 01:43:46.115
the attempt you can
certainly have permission.

01:43:46.116 --> 01:43:47.235
How soon can you start?

01:43:47.236 --> 01:43:48.069
Right away.

01:43:48.070 --> 01:43:49.815
The rocket ship is all fueled and ready.

01:43:49.816 --> 01:43:51.555
Joan, phone Hank and tell me get

01:43:51.556 --> 01:43:54.075
the jets warmed up, we leave right away.

01:43:54.076 --> 01:43:55.925
I want to get started
before there's any chance

01:43:55.926 --> 01:43:57.865
of the news leaking out so Retik won't

01:43:57.866 --> 01:44:00.058
be laying for us when we get there.

01:44:00.059 --> 01:44:03.309
(light dramatic music)

01:44:07.006 --> 01:44:08.455
Well boys, that's it.

01:44:08.456 --> 01:44:10.335
Hope this trip is as easy as your last one.

01:44:10.336 --> 01:44:11.486
Thanks, it should be.

01:44:12.446 --> 01:44:13.446
-Goodbye.
-Goodbye.

01:44:13.446 --> 01:44:14.279
Goodbye, sir.

01:44:19.216 --> 01:44:20.465
Hiya, folks, here we go again.

01:44:20.466 --> 01:44:21.995
Hello, Hank, all set?

01:44:21.996 --> 01:44:22.973
Any time now.

01:44:28.337 --> 01:44:31.170
(engine rumbling)

01:44:38.166 --> 01:44:39.366
Safety belts fastened?

01:44:42.196 --> 01:44:43.166
Fire pilot jets.

01:44:44.067 --> 01:44:46.234
(hissing)

01:44:48.029 --> 01:44:48.862
Fire main jets.

01:45:19.164 --> 01:45:20.715
We're full speed, Hank.

01:45:20.716 --> 01:45:21.965
Set a course for the Moon.

01:45:21.966 --> 01:45:22.799
Right!

01:45:23.870 --> 01:45:27.120
(light dramatic music)

01:45:31.576 --> 01:45:33.673
Take over here, will ya, Ted?

01:45:58.179 --> 01:45:59.279
We're just about here.

01:46:03.676 --> 01:46:05.536
We oughta be down in another two hours.

01:46:08.795 --> 01:46:10.962
(hissing)

01:46:16.176 --> 01:46:18.135
I can see the city now.

01:46:18.136 --> 01:46:19.116
We don't wanna get too close,

01:46:19.117 --> 01:46:21.485
so swing west, Hank and
head to that same canyon.

01:46:21.486 --> 01:46:22.319
Okay.

01:46:29.456 --> 01:46:31.845
We're almost to the canyon now.

01:46:31.846 --> 01:46:33.196
Okay, I'll take her down.

01:46:46.864 --> 01:46:49.031
All right, set her down.

01:46:51.375 --> 01:46:54.125
(dramatic music)

01:47:00.206 --> 01:47:01.645
You sure you don't me to go along?

01:47:01.646 --> 01:47:03.055
No, not this time.

01:47:03.056 --> 01:47:04.435
This is just a scouting trip to try

01:47:04.436 --> 01:47:05.865
to find where they keep the lunarium.

01:47:05.866 --> 01:47:07.315
[Joan] How do you expect to do that?

01:47:07.316 --> 01:47:08.825
Well if I'm lucky I'll
be able to capture one of

01:47:08.826 --> 01:47:11.276
the moon men and get some
information out of him.

01:47:13.770 --> 01:47:17.020
(light dramatic music)

01:47:23.518 --> 01:47:25.685
(buzzing)

01:47:42.670 --> 01:47:43.781
(blasting)

01:47:43.782 --> 01:47:46.532
(dramatic music)

01:48:29.751 --> 01:48:32.150
[Cody] Do you want me
to cut off your air again?

01:48:32.151 --> 01:48:34.505
[Moon Man] No, no.

01:48:34.506 --> 01:48:36.345
[Cody] Where is the lunarium stored?

01:48:36.346 --> 01:48:37.506
[Moon Man] I will tell you.

01:48:38.996 --> 01:48:40.095
Think I'll pass?

01:48:40.096 --> 01:48:42.795
Sure, you'll pass all right,
if that joker told the truth.

01:48:42.796 --> 01:48:45.205
He wasn't any position to lie very well.

01:48:45.206 --> 01:48:46.365
Now it's just lucky I picked up

01:48:46.366 --> 01:48:47.845
one of the men who guard the lunariam.

01:48:47.846 --> 01:48:49.015
If we're gonna get there in time for you

01:48:49.016 --> 01:48:50.896
to take his place we better hurry.

01:48:52.929 --> 01:48:56.179
(light dramatic music)

01:48:58.936 --> 01:49:00.211
It's a little after 9:00.

01:49:00.212 --> 01:49:02.205
I'll go right in, you find a place to hide

01:49:02.206 --> 01:49:03.489
and watch for me to come out.

01:49:03.490 --> 01:49:06.989
[Ted] Okay.

01:49:06.990 --> 01:49:09.240
(creaking)

01:49:20.572 --> 01:49:22.157
[Moon Man] About time you got here.

01:49:22.158 --> 01:49:27.158
[Cody] I was delayed.

01:49:39.793 --> 01:49:41.960
(banging)

01:49:43.283 --> 01:49:45.533
(creaking)

01:50:10.187 --> 01:50:12.354
(buzzing)

01:50:22.076 --> 01:50:22.976
You've got it!

01:50:22.977 --> 01:50:24.905
[Moon Man] Yes, it's so heavy it's going to

01:50:24.906 --> 01:50:27.006
take us a week to lug it back to the ship.

01:50:28.026 --> 01:50:29.226
Get out of sight, quick!

01:50:32.767 --> 01:50:35.600
(engine rumbling)

01:50:47.809 --> 01:50:50.059
(creaking)

01:50:56.871 --> 01:50:57.704
Come on.

01:51:03.000 --> 01:51:06.333
[Moon Man] Parol number six reporting.

01:51:09.175 --> 01:51:12.175
(suspenseful music)

01:51:24.246 --> 01:51:25.396
That is all, very well.

01:51:29.371 --> 01:51:31.621
(rumbling)

01:51:38.642 --> 01:51:39.725
This is patrol number six.

01:51:39.726 --> 01:51:42.349
Somebody stole my car,
send another one quickly.

01:51:50.666 --> 01:51:52.066
[Cody] How's the fuel pressure?

01:51:53.336 --> 01:51:54.286
[Ted] Seems okay.

01:52:23.949 --> 01:52:26.397
[Cody] Make all the speed you can.

01:52:26.398 --> 01:52:27.398
There he is.

01:52:29.330 --> 01:52:30.555
That's right where they're amiss.

01:52:30.556 --> 01:52:33.747
That might stop it.

01:52:33.748 --> 01:52:35.725
(booming)

01:52:35.726 --> 01:52:36.845
[Ted] What was that?

01:52:36.846 --> 01:52:38.015
[Cody] A ray gun blast.

01:52:38.016 --> 01:52:40.306
See what's behind us.

01:52:40.307 --> 01:52:43.057
(dramatic music)

01:52:49.346 --> 01:52:50.825
[Ted] There's another car chasing us.

01:52:50.826 --> 01:52:52.380
We'd better use our gun.

01:52:52.381 --> 01:52:53.805
[Cody] We'll have to turn around to do it.

01:52:53.806 --> 01:52:54.815
There's a bunch of rocks ahead

01:52:54.816 --> 01:52:55.925
that will give us some shelter.

01:52:55.926 --> 01:52:57.810
We'll wait till we get there.

01:52:57.811 --> 01:53:00.811
(suspenseful music)

01:53:03.316 --> 01:53:04.365
[Ted] It's heading for some rocks,

01:53:04.366 --> 01:53:05.466
we'll have to stop it.

01:53:07.263 --> 01:53:09.430
(booming)

01:53:13.606 --> 01:53:16.405
That's our feed pressure line, we're stuck.

01:53:16.406 --> 01:53:17.406
[Ted] I'll say we are.

01:53:17.407 --> 01:53:19.305
[Cody] Pressure's down to nothing.

01:53:19.306 --> 01:53:21.395
[Ted] I can fix this if I have time.

01:53:21.396 --> 01:53:23.755
Fly out and try to stop
them with your grenades.

01:53:23.756 --> 01:53:24.589
[Cody] Okay.

01:53:26.963 --> 01:53:28.395
[Moon Man] They stopped behind a rock,

01:53:28.396 --> 01:53:31.424
but I think I can blast them.

01:53:31.425 --> 01:53:33.675
(blasting)

01:53:34.887 --> 01:53:37.244
(booming)

01:53:37.245 --> 01:53:42.245
(air hissing) (dramatic music)

01:53:49.043 --> 01:53:51.793
(dramatic music)

01:55:27.820 --> 01:55:30.340
[Ted] There's a bunch of rocks ahead
that will give us some shelter.

01:55:31.618 --> 01:55:32.605
[Moon Man] He's heading for some rocks,

01:55:32.606 --> 01:55:33.755
we'll have to stop him.

01:55:35.155 --> 01:55:36.977
(booming)

01:55:36.978 --> 01:55:39.395
(clattering)

01:55:41.786 --> 01:55:44.235
[Ted] That's our feed
pressure line, we're stuck.

01:55:44.236 --> 01:55:45.305
[Cody] I'll say we are.

01:55:45.306 --> 01:55:47.085
[Ted] Pressure's down to nothing.

01:55:47.086 --> 01:55:49.165
I could fix this if I have time.

01:55:49.166 --> 01:55:51.565
Fly out and try to stop
them with your grenades.

01:55:51.566 --> 01:55:52.399
[Cody] Okay.

01:55:54.125 --> 01:55:55.445
[Moon Man] He stopped behind a rock.

01:55:55.446 --> 01:55:57.635
But I think I can blast him.

01:55:57.636 --> 01:56:00.386
(dramatic music)

01:56:01.887 --> 01:56:04.054
(booming)

01:56:11.263 --> 01:56:12.894
(booming)

01:56:12.895 --> 01:56:14.295
(rattling)
-What was that?

01:56:17.565 --> 01:56:20.065
(air hissing)

01:56:42.730 --> 01:56:44.955
We're stuck!
-So is the other car.

01:56:44.956 --> 01:56:49.956
[Moon Man] Let's go after
him with our ray pistols.

01:56:53.796 --> 01:56:55.025
[Cody] Feel better?

01:56:55.026 --> 01:56:56.365
[Ted] Yes.

01:56:56.366 --> 01:56:57.336
Did you stop them?

01:56:57.337 --> 01:56:59.685
[Cody] For a little while,
but I don't know for how long.

01:56:59.686 --> 01:57:01.005
[Ted] You better go out
and see what's happening

01:57:01.006 --> 01:57:03.404
while I try to fix that feed pressure line.

01:57:03.405 --> 01:57:07.222
[Cody] Okay.

01:57:07.223 --> 01:57:09.973
(dramatic music)

01:57:18.161 --> 01:57:20.328
(booming)

01:57:24.359 --> 01:57:26.526
(booming)

01:57:35.636 --> 01:57:36.636
[Ted] Hey!

01:57:53.788 --> 01:57:56.038
(rumbling)

01:58:29.456 --> 01:58:31.115
Get Hank and put this aboard.

01:58:31.116 --> 01:58:33.765
Get set for a takeoff as fast as you can.

01:58:33.766 --> 01:58:35.035
I'll ditch this car.

01:58:35.036 --> 01:58:35.869
[Cody] Right.

01:58:53.070 --> 01:58:53.977
[Hank] Okay we're ready.

01:58:53.977 --> 01:58:54.810
Right.

01:58:56.428 --> 01:58:57.261
[Moon Man] Aren't you going

01:58:57.261 --> 01:58:58.176
to let me go before you leave?

01:58:58.177 --> 01:58:59.885
No we're taking you
with us and you better go

01:58:59.886 --> 01:59:02.555
back to your quarters until we get started.

01:59:02.556 --> 01:59:03.389
Get going!

01:59:10.866 --> 01:59:12.106
Safety belts fastened?

01:59:14.271 --> 01:59:16.281
Fire pilot jets.

01:59:16.282 --> 01:59:18.449
(roaring)

01:59:20.224 --> 01:59:21.474
Fire main jets.

01:59:23.114 --> 01:59:25.281
(hissing)

01:59:42.821 --> 01:59:45.214
Well, we're on our way.

01:59:45.215 --> 01:59:46.996
And am I glad.

01:59:46.997 --> 01:59:48.653
I'll go get us some coffee.

01:59:52.411 --> 01:59:53.275
(thudding)

01:59:53.276 --> 01:59:56.025
(dramatic music)

01:59:58.620 --> 02:00:01.161
(grunting)

02:00:01.162 --> 02:00:03.662
(air hissing)

02:00:16.539 --> 02:00:18.956
(clattering)

02:01:04.964 --> 02:01:07.131
(banging)

02:01:32.219 --> 02:01:34.726
What'll they do with him Hank?

02:01:34.727 --> 02:01:37.196
It's just like a burial at sea, Joan.

02:01:37.197 --> 02:01:41.280
Only his body will float
around in space forever.

02:01:44.914 --> 02:01:46.035
Everything okay, Hank?

02:01:46.036 --> 02:01:47.655
She's under control now.

02:01:47.656 --> 02:01:48.925
Good.

02:01:48.926 --> 02:01:51.503
Make a 180 degree turn and head for home.

02:01:51.504 --> 02:01:52.337
Okay!

02:01:54.353 --> 02:01:57.103
(dramatic music)

02:02:04.015 --> 02:02:06.515
(light music)

02:02:07.576 --> 02:02:09.285
Retik calling Krog.

02:02:09.286 --> 02:02:10.436
Retik calling Krog.

02:02:16.806 --> 02:02:17.946
Retik calling Krog.

02:02:19.896 --> 02:02:21.841
This is Krog, Your Excellency.

02:02:21.842 --> 02:02:23.425
[Retik] The rocket ship
from Earth has been here again

02:02:23.426 --> 02:02:25.835
and has escaped with a supply of lunarium.

02:02:25.836 --> 02:02:27.935
That's serious, now they
can build their own ray guns

02:02:27.936 --> 02:02:29.965
and prevent your invasion from the moon.

02:02:29.966 --> 02:02:31.105
Of course.

02:02:31.106 --> 02:02:33.715
So their ship must not be allowed to land.

02:02:33.716 --> 02:02:35.795
Calculate the time of their arrival

02:02:35.796 --> 02:02:38.385
and have your ray gun set
up ready to blast them.

02:02:38.386 --> 02:02:40.555
This time you must not fail.

02:02:40.556 --> 02:02:44.005
Your own life and the future
of our people are at stake.

02:02:44.006 --> 02:02:45.606
I understand, Your Excellency.

02:02:49.206 --> 02:02:53.086
You heard the orders, there
must be no bumbling this time.

02:02:55.162 --> 02:02:57.412
I will draw up a detailed
plan of operations.

02:03:02.062 --> 02:03:04.812
(dramatic music)

02:03:10.726 --> 02:03:12.165
There we are.

02:03:12.166 --> 02:03:13.607
We ought to be able to
pick up the good ol' Earth

02:03:13.608 --> 02:03:18.608
on a scanning screen pretty quick.

02:03:29.966 --> 02:03:32.056
Here it comes, right when Krog figured.

02:03:37.076 --> 02:03:39.355
Wait'll it turns in for a landing.

02:03:39.356 --> 02:03:40.189
Okay.

02:03:44.157 --> 02:03:46.686
All right, Hank, make your 180 degree turn.

02:03:51.049 --> 02:03:53.299
(blasting)

02:03:57.976 --> 02:03:59.746
Going in for a landing.

02:04:03.276 --> 02:04:06.252
Any time now.

02:04:06.253 --> 02:04:08.420
(booming)

02:04:09.426 --> 02:04:10.675
That was a ray gun blast.

02:04:10.676 --> 02:04:11.926
Take her up again, quick!

02:04:18.846 --> 02:04:20.896
Quite too soon, it wasn't close enough.

02:04:31.486 --> 02:04:34.085
Keep going up, we've
got to stay out of range.

02:04:34.086 --> 02:04:34.946
Okay, but then what?

02:04:34.947 --> 02:04:36.305
We're almost out of fuel.

02:04:36.306 --> 02:04:37.445
Gotta set her down sometime.

02:04:37.446 --> 02:04:38.925
It's probably Graber and Daly

02:04:38.926 --> 02:04:40.405
on a truck with a ray gun.

02:04:40.406 --> 02:04:42.066
I'll try to stop them!

02:04:51.022 --> 02:04:54.323
Still climbing slow,
but it's way out of range.

02:04:54.324 --> 02:04:56.524
Well, they'll have to come down some time.

02:05:01.066 --> 02:05:02.595
Yeah but we're gonna have trouble first.

02:05:02.596 --> 02:05:04.385
Here comes Cody in his flying suit.

02:05:04.386 --> 02:05:05.525
Get him in your sights and blast him

02:05:05.526 --> 02:05:10.034
when he gets close enough.

02:05:10.035 --> 02:05:11.506
(dramatic music)

02:05:11.507 --> 02:05:12.515
If I wait for him to get any closer,

02:05:12.516 --> 02:05:13.426
he'll be right over us.

02:05:13.427 --> 02:05:14.910
Then take a shot at him!

02:05:14.911 --> 02:05:19.828
(booming) (dramatic music)

02:05:29.976 --> 02:05:31.375
Well this is it, folks, we've gotta turn back

02:05:31.376 --> 02:05:34.026
and land before we're clear outta fuel.

02:05:40.613 --> 02:05:42.071
Rocket's coming in again.

02:05:42.072 --> 02:05:43.682
Get set for it.

02:05:43.683 --> 02:05:46.686
This time, wait'll it gets
so close you can't miss.

02:05:46.687 --> 02:05:49.177
(rustling)

02:05:49.178 --> 02:05:52.178
(suspenseful music)

02:06:08.810 --> 02:06:10.977
(banging)

02:06:23.246 --> 02:06:24.766
Through the ray gun at him!

02:06:30.233 --> 02:06:33.095
(booming)

02:06:33.096 --> 02:06:34.785
Forget him, get the rocket.

02:06:34.786 --> 02:06:35.636
It's almost down.

02:06:43.259 --> 02:06:44.092
Now what?

02:06:45.339 --> 02:06:48.693
We gotta get Cody first, give it a blast.

02:06:48.694 --> 02:06:51.555
I can't get at him behind that rock.

02:06:51.556 --> 02:06:56.152
Then hit the cliff above
him and bring it down on him.

02:06:56.153 --> 02:06:58.375
(booming)

02:06:58.376 --> 02:07:01.266
(rumbling)

02:07:01.267 --> 02:07:04.016
(dramatic music)

02:08:49.982 --> 02:08:51.036
(dramatic music) (banging)

02:08:52.836 --> 02:08:53.976
Forget him, get the rocket.

02:08:54.177 --> 02:08:55.626
It's almost down.

02:08:55.982 --> 02:08:56.936
(dramatic music) (banging)

02:08:57.854 --> 02:09:00.282
(banging)

02:09:02.982 --> 02:09:04.199
Now what?

02:09:05.376 --> 02:09:07.576
We gotta get Cody first, give him a blast.

02:09:07.876 --> 02:09:10.166
I can't get at him behind that rock.

02:09:10.567 --> 02:09:13.128
Then hit the cliff above
him and bring it down on him.

02:09:14.928 --> 02:09:17.212
(booming) (rumbling)

02:09:31.706 --> 02:09:32.539
Did that get him?

02:09:33.726 --> 02:09:35.275
Can't tell.

02:09:35.276 --> 02:09:36.715
But we missed the rocket,

02:09:36.716 --> 02:09:39.485
it's already landed on the
other side of the hill.

02:09:39.486 --> 02:09:40.545
Maybe we can blast them before

02:09:40.546 --> 02:09:42.151
they get a chance to unload.

02:09:42.152 --> 02:09:43.439
No, there'll be too many guards there,

02:09:43.440 --> 02:09:45.071
we might lose the ray gun.

02:09:45.072 --> 02:09:50.072
We'd better pull outta here.

02:09:51.316 --> 02:09:54.066
(dramatic music)

02:10:15.603 --> 02:10:18.186
(spooky music)

02:10:19.406 --> 02:10:20.995
This is serious.

02:10:20.996 --> 02:10:22.085
And Cody did escape,

02:10:22.086 --> 02:10:24.465
I heard the announcement over the radio.

02:10:24.466 --> 02:10:25.866
I must report to the moon.

02:10:32.066 --> 02:10:33.046
Krog calling Retik.

02:10:40.716 --> 02:10:42.036
Krog calling Retik.

02:10:44.576 --> 02:10:45.786
Krog calling Retik.

02:10:49.980 --> 02:10:51.070
Come in, Krog.

02:10:51.071 --> 02:10:53.255
I have very bad news, Your Excellency.

02:10:53.256 --> 02:10:54.875
Commando Cody has upset our plans

02:10:54.876 --> 02:10:56.475
for destroying the rocket ship

02:10:56.476 --> 02:10:58.585
and the lunarium has been landed.

02:10:58.586 --> 02:11:00.265
This is intolerable.

02:11:00.266 --> 02:11:03.225
If the Earth people use that
lunarium to build ray guns

02:11:03.226 --> 02:11:05.515
they will be able to repel our invasion.

02:11:05.516 --> 02:11:07.685
[Krog] I realize that, but I did my best.

02:11:07.686 --> 02:11:09.465
Your best is not good enough!

02:11:09.466 --> 02:11:11.245
I'm going to fly down to Earth at once

02:11:11.246 --> 02:11:13.375
and take charge of operations myself.

02:11:13.376 --> 02:11:15.195
I will welcome your help.

02:11:15.196 --> 02:11:16.665
Apparently you need it.

02:11:16.666 --> 02:11:19.735
In the meantime, have your
men go after Commando Cody

02:11:19.736 --> 02:11:22.085
and any other key personnel they can reach.

02:11:22.086 --> 02:11:25.195
We must delay the completion
of any ray guns on Earth

02:11:25.196 --> 02:11:27.795
until my invasion fleet is ready.

02:11:27.796 --> 02:11:28.966
Yes, Your Excellency.

02:11:32.336 --> 02:11:34.525
(dramatic music)

02:11:34.526 --> 02:11:36.856
Cody and his assistants must be destroyed.

02:11:42.216 --> 02:11:43.525
The lunarium arrived safely

02:11:43.526 --> 02:11:44.875
at the government atomic laboratory

02:11:44.876 --> 02:11:46.475
and they've already started converting

02:11:46.476 --> 02:11:48.985
it into a compound suitable
for use in the ray gun.

02:11:48.986 --> 02:11:50.115
How long will that take?

02:11:50.116 --> 02:11:51.315
Some time, I'm afraid.

02:11:51.316 --> 02:11:53.095
The element's entirely
new to our scientists,

02:11:53.096 --> 02:11:53.929
and they'll have to build

02:11:53.930 --> 02:11:55.965
considerable equipment to handle it.

02:11:55.966 --> 02:11:57.025
Well I hope they can get it ready

02:11:57.026 --> 02:11:58.085
before the moon men attack.

02:11:58.086 --> 02:12:00.595
Do you have any idea when
the invasion may be expected?

02:12:00.596 --> 02:12:01.805
No.

02:12:01.806 --> 02:12:03.905
The moon ruler told me
himself he was planning

02:12:03.906 --> 02:12:05.665
the attack, but he didn't say when.

02:12:05.666 --> 02:12:07.435
The time element is vital.

02:12:07.436 --> 02:12:08.695
Let's go over in detail what happened

02:12:08.696 --> 02:12:10.065
on your trip to the moon and perhaps

02:12:10.066 --> 02:12:12.795
we can find some clue to
when they plan to strike.

02:12:12.796 --> 02:12:13.629
All right.

02:12:14.606 --> 02:12:17.265
Well, our passage through
space was uneventful.

02:12:17.266 --> 02:12:19.865
The rocket ship functioned perfectly.

02:12:19.866 --> 02:12:21.305
When we reached the moon,

02:12:21.306 --> 02:12:23.699
I decided to go on a scouting trip.

02:12:23.700 --> 02:12:27.198
(light suspenseful music)

02:12:27.199 --> 02:12:29.866
(door creaking)

02:12:33.776 --> 02:12:35.236
Welcome, Commando Cody.

02:12:43.953 --> 02:12:46.605
I am Retik, ruler of the moon.

02:12:46.606 --> 02:12:48.315
Apparently you were expecting me.

02:12:48.316 --> 02:12:49.325
Of course.

02:12:49.326 --> 02:12:51.915
For many years our radio
has kept us informed

02:12:51.916 --> 02:12:54.475
of the events on Earth, and my men there

02:12:54.476 --> 02:12:57.125
have advised me of your every move.

02:12:57.126 --> 02:12:59.155
[Cody] I see you have adopted our language.

02:12:59.156 --> 02:13:00.185
Yes.

02:13:00.186 --> 02:13:02.875
All our people are required to speak English

02:13:02.876 --> 02:13:05.426
so we can operate more
efficiently in your country.

02:13:06.496 --> 02:13:08.085
Do you mind telling me why your men

02:13:08.086 --> 02:13:10.925
are carrying out that campaign
of destruction on Earth?

02:13:10.926 --> 02:13:11.935
Not at all.

02:13:11.936 --> 02:13:13.845
They are merely softening up your defenses

02:13:13.846 --> 02:13:15.596
for our impending invasion.

02:13:16.436 --> 02:13:19.005
[Cody] Why do you want to invade the earth?

02:13:19.006 --> 02:13:20.625
'Cause the atmosphere on the Moon

02:13:20.626 --> 02:13:23.335
has become so thin and dry it is impossible

02:13:23.336 --> 02:13:27.395
for us to raise food except
in pressurized greenhouses.

02:13:27.396 --> 02:13:29.865
And none of us can move
outside without helmets.

02:13:29.866 --> 02:13:33.025
So we are planning a mass
migration to your world.

02:13:33.026 --> 02:13:36.165
You'll find that conquering
the Earth isn't so simple.

02:13:36.166 --> 02:13:37.975
Ah, but it will be.

02:13:37.976 --> 02:13:40.535
Because of our atomic weapons.

02:13:40.536 --> 02:13:43.225
On the Moon we have an element, lunarium,

02:13:43.226 --> 02:13:45.715
which is far superior to uranium

02:13:45.716 --> 02:13:48.045
as a base for atomic reactions.

02:13:48.046 --> 02:13:52.025
And we can completely control
the force of these reactions,

02:13:52.026 --> 02:13:54.685
enabling us to build atomic weapons ranging

02:13:54.686 --> 02:13:57.966
from huge canon to these small ray pistols.

02:14:04.306 --> 02:14:05.535
It's very considerate of you

02:14:05.536 --> 02:14:07.735
to give me all this information.

02:14:07.736 --> 02:14:10.865
You deserve some reward
for your long journey,

02:14:10.866 --> 02:14:13.065
but unfortunately I cannot permit

02:14:13.066 --> 02:14:15.085
you to return to Earth with it.

02:14:15.086 --> 02:14:17.236
Maybe I have something to say about that.

02:14:21.517 --> 02:14:23.767
(whirring)

02:14:25.176 --> 02:14:28.285
So much for the
effectiveness of your weapons.

02:14:28.286 --> 02:14:31.119
Now I will demonstrate one of ours.

02:14:34.493 --> 02:14:35.767
(dramatic music)

02:14:35.768 --> 02:14:37.935
(booming)

02:14:40.778 --> 02:14:45.262
Seize him!

02:14:45.263 --> 02:14:47.513
(thudding)

02:14:52.819 --> 02:14:55.236
(clattering)

02:15:17.428 --> 02:15:19.595
(booming)

02:15:33.368 --> 02:15:34.755
We decided we would need a ray gun

02:15:34.756 --> 02:15:36.815
if we were to attack the city.

02:15:36.816 --> 02:15:39.085
So the next day, Ted and
I went back and turned

02:15:39.086 --> 02:15:41.286
nitrous oxide into their ventilating system.

02:15:42.186 --> 02:15:44.565
When Retik and his guard became unconscious,

02:15:44.566 --> 02:15:47.195
Ted waited while I went
in and got a ray gun.

02:15:47.196 --> 02:15:51.025
But before we could... (dramatic music)

02:15:51.026 --> 02:15:52.176
They're still after us.

02:15:53.046 --> 02:15:53.879
Let's go.

02:15:55.282 --> 02:15:57.532
(rumbling)

02:16:06.976 --> 02:16:11.859
[Ted] That looks like a
cave, let's get in there.

02:16:32.267 --> 02:16:33.636
[Moon Man] We can't follow them in there.

02:16:34.516 --> 02:16:36.455
Set the ray gun at constant heat.

02:16:36.456 --> 02:16:38.575
We'll melt the cliff and bury them alive.

02:16:38.576 --> 02:16:39.545
[Moon Man] Right.

02:16:39.546 --> 02:16:42.295
(dramatic music)

02:17:11.298 --> 02:17:12.527
[Ted] What's that?

02:17:12.528 --> 02:17:13.361
[Cody] They've turned the ray gun

02:17:13.362 --> 02:17:15.655
to the side of the cave
and there's no way to run.

02:17:15.656 --> 02:17:17.590
Let's get back as far as we can.

02:17:17.591 --> 02:17:22.591
Never mind the gun!

02:17:32.749 --> 02:17:34.999
(rumbling)

02:17:37.046 --> 02:17:38.805
[Ted] Maybe we can get out along that side.

02:17:38.806 --> 02:17:40.195
[Cody] But what about that tank?

02:17:40.196 --> 02:17:42.296
[Ted] We may be able to take care of it.

02:17:55.786 --> 02:17:58.815
Let's try this way.

02:17:58.816 --> 02:18:00.195
I hated to lose that ray gun,

02:18:00.196 --> 02:18:02.305
but it would only have
been good for a few shots

02:18:02.306 --> 02:18:04.165
without another charge of lunarium.

02:18:04.166 --> 02:18:05.595
And now that we have a lunarium,

02:18:05.596 --> 02:18:08.005
we can build our own ray guns and pistols.

02:18:08.006 --> 02:18:08.846
Yes.

02:18:08.847 --> 02:18:10.896
We brought back one of their ray pistols.

02:18:23.316 --> 02:18:24.335
[Henderson] Looks fairly simple.

02:18:24.336 --> 02:18:26.075
[Cody] Yes, would you
like me to take it apart

02:18:26.076 --> 02:18:27.195
to show you how it works?

02:18:27.196 --> 02:18:28.126
[Henderson] Please.

02:18:31.967 --> 02:18:34.717
(dramatic music)

02:18:56.293 --> 02:18:58.055
There's the intake for
the air conditioning system.

02:18:58.056 --> 02:18:59.856
Put the hose in and turn the gas on.

02:19:11.591 --> 02:19:13.285
(whirring)

02:19:13.286 --> 02:19:14.425
Let's find a spot where we can watch

02:19:14.426 --> 02:19:16.406
the window in case anyone tries to get out.

02:19:21.639 --> 02:19:24.185
We must start manufacturing
these weapons at once.

02:19:24.186 --> 02:19:25.885
Wouldn't it be better to save the lunarium

02:19:25.886 --> 02:19:27.035
for bigger guns?

02:19:27.036 --> 02:19:29.805
They're what we'll need to stop
an invasion by rocket ships.

02:19:29.806 --> 02:19:33.665
Excuse me, but isn't getting
awfully stuffy in here?

02:19:33.666 --> 02:19:35.635
I'll open a window.

02:19:35.636 --> 02:19:38.386
(dramatic music)

02:19:42.052 --> 02:19:47.052
(banging) (glass shattering)

02:19:58.876 --> 02:20:01.176
You better get her out
of here, Mr. Henderson.

02:20:10.421 --> 02:20:12.671
(thudding)

02:20:17.588 --> 02:20:18.921
It won't open!

02:20:28.879 --> 02:20:31.129
(thudding)

02:20:38.396 --> 02:20:41.146
(dramatic music)

02:22:18.223 --> 02:22:21.473
(light dramatic music)

02:22:22.595 --> 02:22:24.462
(hissing)

02:22:24.509 --> 02:22:25.631
(banging)

02:22:25.831 --> 02:22:29.631
You better get her out
of here, Mr. Henderson.

02:22:41.240 --> 02:22:43.490
(rattling)

02:22:44.169 --> 02:22:45.502
This won't open!

02:22:55.374 --> 02:22:57.624
(thudding)

02:23:02.940 --> 02:23:05.607
(alarm ringing)

02:23:07.506 --> 02:23:09.345
We'd better get outta
here, that'll bring the cops.

02:23:09.346 --> 02:23:10.596
We can't yet.

02:23:30.458 --> 02:23:33.093
(clanking)

02:23:33.094 --> 02:23:35.344
(sniffing)

02:23:54.079 --> 02:23:55.941
Well, I guess that finished him.

02:23:55.942 --> 02:23:57.692
Let's get outta here.

02:24:01.496 --> 02:24:03.257
I'm all right now.

02:24:03.258 --> 02:24:04.670
He seems to be coming around all right.

02:24:04.671 --> 02:24:06.484
Somebody took a shot at me from outside.

02:24:06.485 --> 02:24:07.970
I'm going to go look for them.

02:24:07.971 --> 02:24:09.881
You'd better stay here with him.

02:24:09.882 --> 02:24:13.132
(light dramatic music)

02:24:18.900 --> 02:24:19.899
(banging)

02:24:19.900 --> 02:24:21.591
It's Graber and Daly.

02:24:21.592 --> 02:24:22.425
Come on!

02:24:24.478 --> 02:24:26.145
-I'll drive.
-Okay.

02:24:40.136 --> 02:24:40.977
[Henderson] What's the matter?

02:24:40.977 --> 02:24:41.829
Somebody stole my car,

02:24:41.830 --> 02:24:45.079
I've gotta get to a phone to report it.

02:24:49.373 --> 02:24:54.085
[Graber] There's a car
following us, keep rolling.

02:24:54.086 --> 02:24:56.253
(banging)

02:25:01.498 --> 02:25:03.748
We'll have to get closer.

02:25:06.886 --> 02:25:09.532
[Dispatch] Calling all
cars, calling all cars.

02:25:09.533 --> 02:25:11.043
A black sedan has been stolen from

02:25:11.044 --> 02:25:12.893
in front of Cody Laboratory.

02:25:12.894 --> 02:25:14.694
Last seen going north, get after it.

02:25:15.554 --> 02:25:17.534
Cody must've taken the cop's car.

02:25:17.535 --> 02:25:19.524
I hope they take after him instead of us.

02:25:21.054 --> 02:25:23.971
(engines rumbling)

02:25:29.644 --> 02:25:30.484
We've got some help,

02:25:30.485 --> 02:25:32.953
there's some motor cops right behind us.

02:25:32.954 --> 02:25:34.613
What if the cops are on our side?

02:25:34.614 --> 02:25:38.043
All we have to do is stay
ahead of Cody a little longer.

02:25:38.044 --> 02:25:40.544
(gun banging)

02:25:49.027 --> 02:25:50.027
I'm out of shells.

02:25:56.504 --> 02:25:59.384
Try to get alongside and
I'll use that gas grenade.

02:26:07.909 --> 02:26:08.742
He's catching up with us.

02:26:14.968 --> 02:26:17.553
(thudding)

02:26:17.554 --> 02:26:19.434
Try again, that threw me off balance.

02:26:24.505 --> 02:26:26.672
(banging)

02:26:32.785 --> 02:26:35.035
(coughing)

02:26:38.639 --> 02:26:41.556
(tires screeching)

02:26:43.478 --> 02:26:45.663
[Joan] I can't see a thing!

02:26:45.664 --> 02:26:47.603
Something's wrong with their car.

02:26:47.604 --> 02:26:48.437
Slow down.

02:26:51.597 --> 02:26:53.847
(crashing)

02:26:54.814 --> 02:26:56.204
Get out with your hands up.

02:27:06.004 --> 02:27:06.874
[Officer] We'll handle this.

02:27:06.874 --> 02:27:07.864
Wait a minute, officer.

02:27:07.865 --> 02:27:09.003
I'm Commando Cody.

02:27:09.004 --> 02:27:11.253
These men tried to murder
us in my laboratory.

02:27:11.254 --> 02:27:13.413
Yeah, well all I know is
that you stole the police car,

02:27:13.414 --> 02:27:15.313
so I'm taking the whole bunch a
you down to the station.

02:27:15.314 --> 02:27:16.576
Come on, get in the car.

02:27:16.577 --> 02:27:19.655
All of you.

02:27:19.656 --> 02:27:21.113
Certainly, officer.

02:27:21.114 --> 02:27:22.474
That's a good idea.

02:27:28.418 --> 02:27:30.603
You must've done some fast
talking to get out of that.

02:27:30.604 --> 02:27:32.763
No, as soon as I convinced them who I was

02:27:32.764 --> 02:27:33.833
everything was all right.

02:27:33.834 --> 02:27:35.983
Did you find out anything
from Graber and Daly?

02:27:35.984 --> 02:27:37.103
Not a thing.

02:27:37.104 --> 02:27:38.813
They denied they ever used the ray gun

02:27:38.814 --> 02:27:39.973
or that they have anything to do

02:27:39.974 --> 02:27:41.623
with the planned invasion form the moon.

02:27:41.624 --> 02:27:43.223
But you can testify that you've seen

02:27:43.224 --> 02:27:44.593
them using the ray gun.

02:27:44.594 --> 02:27:46.273
I could but I'm not going to.

02:27:46.274 --> 02:27:47.653
What?

02:27:47.654 --> 02:27:48.983
My testimony could convict them,

02:27:48.984 --> 02:27:50.413
but what good would it do?

02:27:50.414 --> 02:27:52.433
They're just hired thugs.

02:27:52.434 --> 02:27:54.073
And whoever is boss of
this show could easily

02:27:54.074 --> 02:27:55.793
hire someone else to operate the ray guns.

02:27:55.794 --> 02:27:58.783
But it's ridiculous to
turn those murderers loose.

02:27:58.784 --> 02:27:59.624
I know it looks that way,

02:27:59.625 --> 02:28:01.513
but it's the only way to
locate their headquarters

02:28:01.514 --> 02:28:03.303
and perhaps smash the whole gang.

02:28:03.304 --> 02:28:04.703
How do you figure that?

02:28:04.704 --> 02:28:06.783
Well, I've instructed
the police to release them

02:28:06.784 --> 02:28:08.513
and trail them until they leave town.

02:28:08.514 --> 02:28:10.742
Then they'll radio me and I'll take over.

02:28:10.743 --> 02:28:13.833
(light dramatic music)

02:28:13.834 --> 02:28:16.833
Still can't figure out how
we got out of that so easy.

02:28:16.834 --> 02:28:17.667
Yeah.

02:28:17.668 --> 02:28:19.317
Did seem kind of phony.

02:28:28.144 --> 02:28:30.174
There's a car back there
and it might be tailing us.

02:28:31.814 --> 02:28:32.993
Do we run for it?

02:28:32.994 --> 02:28:33.874
Not yet.

02:28:33.875 --> 02:28:36.643
Take it easy till we
make sure he's after us.

02:28:36.644 --> 02:28:38.593
[Dispatch] Calling Commando Cody.

02:28:38.594 --> 02:28:39.704
Calling Commando Cody.

02:28:42.104 --> 02:28:43.793
This is Commando Cody, come in.

02:28:43.794 --> 02:28:44.983
[Dispatch] Your men are headed out of town

02:28:44.984 --> 02:28:46.683
on Highway number 19.

02:28:46.684 --> 02:28:48.823
They are driving at a
moderate rate of speed.

02:28:48.824 --> 02:28:51.853
They should pass the city
limits in about five minutes.

02:28:51.854 --> 02:28:53.244
I'll get out there right away.

02:28:55.564 --> 02:28:56.863
Well, I hope it works.

02:28:56.864 --> 02:28:57.697
Good luck.

02:28:57.698 --> 02:28:59.083
You're sure you won't need me?

02:28:59.084 --> 02:29:03.811
No, Ted, but thanks anyway.

02:29:13.998 --> 02:29:15.316
(blasting)

02:29:15.317 --> 02:29:18.067
(dramatic music)

02:29:29.937 --> 02:29:32.755
That car turned off so I
guess it wasn't following us.

02:29:32.756 --> 02:29:34.062
Head for the cave.

02:29:34.063 --> 02:29:39.063
Right.

02:31:15.164 --> 02:31:18.023
I can't understand why
they let you off so easy,

02:31:18.024 --> 02:31:20.723
but it's very fortunate
you came back when you did.

02:31:20.724 --> 02:31:22.123
Retik has arrived.

02:31:22.124 --> 02:31:24.703
He came down in his personal rocket ship.

02:31:24.704 --> 02:31:26.463
He landed it in the cave in the east side

02:31:26.464 --> 02:31:28.463
of the old Mount Henry mine.

02:31:28.464 --> 02:31:30.553
I just spoke to him by radio.

02:31:30.554 --> 02:31:32.953
He wants us to arrange for four more trucks

02:31:32.954 --> 02:31:36.023
and eight men to operate the
ray guns he brought with him.

02:31:36.024 --> 02:31:39.704
[Graber] Okay, we'll go to town and get 'em.

02:31:44.571 --> 02:31:46.008
[Cody] Get those hands higher.

02:31:46.009 --> 02:31:47.845
(dramatic music)

02:31:47.846 --> 02:31:50.263
(clattering)

02:31:54.954 --> 02:31:57.204
(grunting)

02:32:00.147 --> 02:32:02.397
(thudding)

02:33:29.702 --> 02:33:31.952
(crashing)

02:33:37.512 --> 02:33:42.095
(sizzling) (screaming)

02:33:46.372 --> 02:33:48.872
(gun banging)

02:33:55.597 --> 02:33:57.847
(sizzling)

02:34:01.618 --> 02:34:04.368
(dramatic music)

02:34:13.752 --> 02:34:16.502
(dramatic music)

02:34:31.785 --> 02:34:34.368
(spooky music)

02:35:38.817 --> 02:35:43.159
(dramatic music) (clattering)

02:35:43.160 --> 02:35:45.410
(thudding)

02:35:47.658 --> 02:35:49.908
(grunting)

02:36:00.425 --> 02:36:05.008
(sizzling) (screaming)

02:36:09.273 --> 02:36:11.773
(gun banging)

02:36:18.737 --> 02:36:20.987
(sizzling)

02:36:29.713 --> 02:36:30.650
They're both finished.

02:36:30.651 --> 02:36:33.150
[Daly] So what do we do now?

02:36:34.014 --> 02:36:35.973
This is Retik, ruler of the Moon.

02:36:35.974 --> 02:36:38.193
You will carry out Krog's orders.

02:36:38.194 --> 02:36:39.803
Get the men and the trucks necessary

02:36:39.804 --> 02:36:42.594
to operate my ray guns and
bring them here at once!

02:37:21.689 --> 02:37:25.522
(dramatic instrumental music)

02:37:36.509 --> 02:37:37.893
And there was enough metal in my flying suit

02:37:37.894 --> 02:37:40.633
to partially ground the current
so I was only knocked out,

02:37:40.634 --> 02:37:42.173
but the other man was killed instantly.

02:37:42.174 --> 02:37:43.373
From what you've told us,

02:37:43.374 --> 02:37:45.343
he must've been the leader
of the Moon forces here.

02:37:45.344 --> 02:37:46.453
I think so.

02:37:46.454 --> 02:37:48.733
But now that Retik is on
Earth, he'll take command.

02:37:48.734 --> 02:37:50.653
And if Graber and Daly
carry out their orders,

02:37:50.654 --> 02:37:52.933
he'll soon have a strong
force of men and ray guns.

02:37:52.934 --> 02:37:55.703
Then we must capture him
before he can get organized.

02:37:55.704 --> 02:37:58.773
If he has ray guns there, it won't be easy.

02:37:58.774 --> 02:38:00.103
No, but at least we can get the ray gun

02:38:00.104 --> 02:38:01.783
in Krog's cave and use it ourselves.

02:38:01.784 --> 02:38:03.463
I'll arrange to have it picked up at once.

02:38:03.464 --> 02:38:04.783
If you will have it mounted on a truck

02:38:04.784 --> 02:38:06.963
it can be taken directly
from there to the mine.

02:38:06.964 --> 02:38:08.303
Ted and I will go out and scout around

02:38:08.304 --> 02:38:10.683
so we can move in on them as
soon as the ray gun gets there.

02:38:10.684 --> 02:38:12.593
I'll get it to you as quickly as possible.

02:38:12.594 --> 02:38:15.444
Yes, sir.

02:38:17.836 --> 02:38:19.973
Do you know exactly where
the Mount Henry mine is?

02:38:19.974 --> 02:38:21.433
Yes, it's an old abandoned one.

02:38:21.434 --> 02:38:22.838
It has two entrances and a...

02:38:22.839 --> 02:38:25.873
(phone ringing)

02:38:25.874 --> 02:38:26.774
Cody Laboratory.

02:38:27.774 --> 02:38:28.607
Yes, he's here.

02:38:30.224 --> 02:38:31.094
Hello?

02:38:31.095 --> 02:38:33.153
This is the bartender
at Al's Cafe, Mr. Cody.

02:38:33.154 --> 02:38:33.987
[Cody] Yes?

02:38:34.884 --> 02:38:37.773
Those two men you asked me
to watch for just came in.

02:38:37.774 --> 02:38:39.753
They're talking to some other fellas.

02:38:39.754 --> 02:38:41.943
Looks like they're tryin' to work up a deal.

02:38:41.944 --> 02:38:45.573
We'll be right down.

02:38:45.574 --> 02:38:47.803
Graber and Daly are at Al's Cafe.

02:38:47.804 --> 02:38:49.223
We have time to pick them up and still get

02:38:49.224 --> 02:38:50.674
to the mine before the truck.

02:39:01.714 --> 02:39:03.114
That's their car, all right.

02:39:09.019 --> 02:39:11.769
(dramatic music)

02:39:16.841 --> 02:39:17.691
Get to your feet.

02:39:21.534 --> 02:39:22.367
Search him.

02:39:27.540 --> 02:39:31.346
(thudding) (dramatic music)

02:39:31.347 --> 02:39:33.597
(grunting)

02:39:41.326 --> 02:39:43.743
(clattering)

02:40:05.482 --> 02:40:07.732
(crashing)

02:40:15.586 --> 02:40:17.836
(thudding)

02:40:45.349 --> 02:40:46.182
Come on, now.

02:40:46.183 --> 02:40:49.182
(suspenseful music)

02:41:11.926 --> 02:41:14.676
They're after us, keep rolling!

02:41:17.117 --> 02:41:19.617
(gun banging)

02:42:11.635 --> 02:42:14.552
(tires screeching)

02:42:16.197 --> 02:42:18.780
(horn honking)

02:42:20.025 --> 02:42:24.442
(crashing) (booming)

02:42:32.364 --> 02:42:34.033
No chance of getting them out of that.

02:42:34.034 --> 02:42:34.984
No.

02:42:34.985 --> 02:42:36.034
Let's go after Retik.

02:42:58.234 --> 02:42:59.067
Everything all right?

02:42:59.067 --> 02:42:59.944
Seems to be.

02:42:59.944 --> 02:43:00.864
We were delayed getting here

02:43:00.865 --> 02:43:03.033
and I don't know what the
set up is in the mine.

02:43:03.034 --> 02:43:04.783
So you stay here with the gun
while we do some scouting.

02:43:04.784 --> 02:43:05.617
Yes, sir.

02:43:18.984 --> 02:43:20.703
Should be here by now.

02:43:20.704 --> 02:43:21.537
Go out to the mine entrance

02:43:21.538 --> 02:43:22.873
and see if there's any sign of them.

02:43:22.874 --> 02:43:23.707
Yes sir.

02:43:37.944 --> 02:43:39.294
Let's take a look inside.

02:43:47.373 --> 02:43:52.373
(suspenseful music) (gun banging)

02:44:45.129 --> 02:44:47.379
(thudding)

02:44:53.866 --> 02:44:57.283
You take that tunnel, I'll take this one!

02:45:09.457 --> 02:45:11.707
(blasting)

02:45:23.744 --> 02:45:26.084
He's getting away in his
rocket, let's get to the truck.

02:45:44.589 --> 02:45:45.824
Get the gun ready, quick!

02:46:01.768 --> 02:46:03.935
(booming)

02:46:10.570 --> 02:46:12.703
Now that Retik's dead, we feel sure there's

02:46:12.704 --> 02:46:15.884
no immediate danger of any
enemy invasion from the moon.

02:46:15.885 --> 02:46:18.383
And we'll have time to
build an adequate defense.

02:46:18.384 --> 02:46:19.843
Will you want us to make another trip to

02:46:19.844 --> 02:46:21.933
the moon to see what's going on?

02:46:21.934 --> 02:46:22.904
I don't think so now that

02:46:22.905 --> 02:46:24.483
the moon men's attack has failed.

02:46:24.484 --> 02:46:25.803
We can make the whole story public

02:46:25.804 --> 02:46:28.493
and the military
authorities can take charge.

02:46:28.494 --> 02:46:30.933
But we will need more of
your rocket ships, Commando,

02:46:30.934 --> 02:46:32.713
so I suggest you make plans for going

02:46:32.714 --> 02:46:35.203
into their manufacture on a large scale.

02:46:35.204 --> 02:46:38.453
Before we get started on
ships using regular rocket fuel,

02:46:38.454 --> 02:46:41.473
let's do some experimenting
with atomic power from lunarium.

02:46:41.474 --> 02:46:43.303
That might be pretty hard to control.

02:46:43.304 --> 02:46:45.043
No, I've got it all figured out.

02:46:45.044 --> 02:46:46.823
Stand back, please.

02:46:46.824 --> 02:46:50.133
Look, by setting the controls
on this model rocket,

02:46:50.134 --> 02:46:53.114
I can make it slowly circle
the room and come right back.

02:46:54.074 --> 02:46:54.907
Watch.

02:46:57.194 --> 02:46:58.027
Here we go!

02:46:59.226 --> 02:47:01.393
(hissing)

02:47:05.080 --> 02:47:07.497
(shattering)

02:47:09.034 --> 02:47:11.463
I thought you said it
was going to slowly circle

02:47:11.464 --> 02:47:12.614
the room and come back.

02:47:14.664 --> 02:47:16.562
At least it did come back.

02:47:16.563 --> 02:47:18.813
(laughing)

02:47:19.648 --> 02:47:23.231
(light instrumental music)
